window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["story-v-y1v4-index"]=[{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p10-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"inner","w":"karuizawa-kei","q":"ch 1  karuizawa kei s soliloquy volume cold open  karuizawa s first person soliloquy  alone post shower at the mirror  no other character appears  and p 11 carries no prose   in the end  nothing changed even after i came to this school   no  that s wrong  maybe i never had any intention of changing   my life was destroyed because of that nightmarish day  i lost my youth  my friends  and even myself   the most important thing is protecting myself  i ll do whatever it takes","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p10-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p10-1\">Ch.1: Karuizawa Kei’s Soliloquy<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.10–11<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Volume cold open: Karuizawa’s first-person soliloquy, alone post-shower at the mirror; no other character appears, and p.11 carries no prose.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “In the end, nothing changed even after I came to this school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “No, that’s wrong… Maybe I never had any intention of changing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “My life was destroyed because of that nightmarish day. I lost my youth, my friends, and even myself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Opens by measuring herself against the class: she is certain “none of the boys or girls like me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Claims the knowing no longer hurts, then turns it outward: “Because for some reason, I want them to feel that way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> At the mirror she grips the sink and vomits at “that old wound on my side” — the page ties her self-loathing to an unnamed past and never says what happened.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “The most important thing is protecting myself. I’ll do whatever it takes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Closing self-assessment: “I’m a parasite, a weak creature that can’t survive on its own.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Translation defect kept as printed: “Why did I have to have to go through” — the verb is doubled.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Blank/short scan page: running footer only; no prose to cite.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p20-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.0: she reclaims the table<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p12-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 0  the cabin reverie and the horikita bridge three days after the island test  the cruise ship respite  ayanokoji s cabin reverie  hirata s interruption  and the deck lunch that follows   sigh  if only i had the power to rotate the earth on its axis myself   i ll pass  i don t think i m on especially good terms with karuizawa s group   well  i don t particularly dislike the idea  but  didn t you already promise karuizawa   but even if i can bring you both together  things won t be that easy  horikita is difficult","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p12-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: the cabin reverie and the Horikita bridge<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.12–20<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Three days after the island test, the cruise-ship respite; Ayanokōji’s cabin reverie, Hirata’s interruption, and the deck lunch that follows.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Sigh. If only I had the power to rotate the earth on its axis myself…”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I’ll pass. I don’t think I’m on especially good terms with Karuizawa’s group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Well, I don’t particularly dislike the idea, but… Didn’t you already promise Karuizawa?”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> The rule he entered school under: “Contact with anyone outside is forbidden until graduation.” Chabashira’s leverage rides on it — she threatened to expel him from this paradise unless he works toward Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> A “little devil” perched on his shoulder whispers that “It’s better to get them before they get you”; he spends a second imagining forcing Chabashira to resign, then returns to blank thinking.<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Rates the boys aboard as “beasts—sex-starved carnivores” waiting like predators while the girls chatter — his anthropology of the vacation mood.<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Grades the friendship tiers: at the bottom strata, “low-level friends are only invited ten percent of the time” — and he is the lowly friend.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Asks after Karuizawa’s recovered underwear and is satisfied with Hirata’s quiet resolution of the fiasco.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads Hirata’s invitation as carrying “some kind of ulterior motive” before the ask lands.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But even if I can bring you both together, things won’t be that easy. Horikita is difficult.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Takes the go-between job while admitting he usually just goes along with whatever Horikita says — “I’ve never really forced my opinion on her.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Executes his “Speedy Escape” the moment Karuizawa’s group closes ranks over Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Pressed into service as the Horikita bridge over lunch; he takes the ask but not the urgency.<span class=\"pg\">p.13–20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Declines her group, then watches her reclaim Hirata anyway.<span class=\"pg\">p.14, 20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The subject of Hirata’s request; he warns she will shut down if she senses manipulation.<span class=\"pg\">p.17–19<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p21-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.1: the Kōenji corridor and Sakura’s call<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4-p12-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"ch 2  the class a leverage  named twice named in ayanokoji s cabin reverie   the leverage that brought him to class a s track","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v4-p12-1\">Ch.2: the Class A leverage, named twice<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.12, p.34<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in Ayanokōji’s cabin reverie — the leverage that brought him to Class A’s track.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> The threat that binds him: she “threatened to expel me from this paradise” unless he works toward Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narrator contrasts her with Mashima: where she seems “unmotivated and unnaturally uncooperative,” he is “impossible to read.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Still holds him with the Class A ultimatum three days after the island test.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p13-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 2  2 0  he pulls ayanokoji to lunch ship cabin  he draws ayanokoji out of his sea gazing and steers him toward lunch  cancelling karuizawa s plan to do it   hmm  you haven t been in the room all this time  have you   you might make more friends if you were a little more proactive  ayanokouji kun  though i suppose it s none of my business   that s not true  though  i mean  you have sudou kun and the guys  and horikita san   i m planning to meet up with karuizawa san and the others at 12 30 to have lunch  do you want to come with  i think it ll be really fun   i can understand that you re feeling hesitant  that s exactly why i want you to rely on me   i can eat with karuizawa san and the others any time  but i haven t really had many opportunities to eat together with you  ayanokouji kun   thank you for helping on the deserted island  i m sorry i didn t thank you enough for helping to find the culprit  ayanokouji kun   even so  i m grateful to you for helping","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p13-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: he pulls Ayanokōji to lunch<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.13–16<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ship cabin: he draws Ayanokōji out of his sea-gazing and steers him toward lunch, cancelling Karuizawa’s plan to do it.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Hmm? You haven’t been in the room all this time, have you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “You might make more friends if you were a little more proactive, Ayanokouji-kun. Though I suppose it’s none of my business.”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “That’s not true, though. I mean, you have Sudou-kun and the guys, and Horikita-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m planning to meet up with Karuizawa-san and the others at 12:30 to have lunch. Do you want to come with? I think it’ll be really fun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Wears “that eternal, optimistic smile” and won’t leave a lone person alone; pushes past the refusals.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can understand that you’re feeling hesitant. That’s exactly why I want you to rely on me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can eat with Karuizawa-san and the others any time, but I haven’t really had many opportunities to eat together with you, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Calls Karuizawa to cancel on the spot, despite Ayanokōji’s half-hearted protests.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you for helping on the deserted island. I’m sorry I didn’t thank you enough for helping to find the culprit, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even so, I’m grateful to you for helping.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Cancels their lunch without flinching; Ayanokōji expects her to blame him later, and he doesn’t seem to care.<span class=\"pg\">p.14–15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p17-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.0: the ask, be the bridge to Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p13-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"sudou-ken","q":"ch 2  2 0  a passing mention in hirata s inventory named once at the cabin lunch  in hirata s list of the people who treat ayanokoji as a friend","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p13-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: a passing mention in Hirata’s inventory<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.13<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once at the cabin lunch, in Hirata’s list of the people who treat Ayanokōji as a friend.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hirata’s line carries him: “you have Sudou-kun and the guys, and Horikita-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p43-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: a passing mention in the comprehension sketch<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p16-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ch 2  2 0  a passing mention as the culprit named once as the underwear culprit  ayanokoji asks whether karuizawa got hers back","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p16-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: a passing mention as the culprit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.16<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once as the underwear culprit; Ayanokōji asks whether Karuizawa got hers back.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hirata confirms the fallout: naming her resolved things — “When she heard Ibuki-san was the culprit, things went smoothly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p68-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.0–§3.1: the café shadow and the Rabbit holdout<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p17-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune karuizawa-kei hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 2  2 0  the ask  be the bridge to horikita top deck restaurant  over lunch he finally names his ask   ayanokoji as the bridge to horikita   honestly  there s something i d like your advice on   i wondered if you would act as a bridge to help reach horikita san  after all  class d will have to come together and work hard in the future  and i think horikita san will be indispensable   yes  i do understand  of course  horikita san only opens herself up to you  ayanokouji kun   i should probably reconsider how to do this  horikita san seems very fastidious and hypercritical  how do you manage to get along with her  ayanokouji kun   my plan was really short sighted   when ayanokoji calls the timing too soon   sorry  i invited you out to eat and made it all about me  well  let s eat  shall we","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p17-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p17-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: the ask, be the bridge to Horikita<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.17–20<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Top-deck restaurant: over lunch he finally names his ask — Ayanokōji as the bridge to Horikita.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Honestly, there’s something I’d like your advice on.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “I wondered if you would act as a bridge to help reach Horikita-san. After all, Class D will have to come together and work hard in the future, and I think Horikita-san will be indispensable.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Yes. I do understand, of course. Horikita-san only opens herself up to you, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Wants his own hand hidden — “Then, pretend I never spoke to you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> “But I can’t come up with anything else right now. I don’t think I have the confidence to speak with Horikita-san, let alone persuade her. This is my last resort.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I should probably reconsider how to do this. Horikita-san seems very fastidious and hypercritical. How do you manage to get along with her, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Has “over forty friends” yet is frustrated at missing a connection with one particular student.<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My plan was really short-sighted.” (when Ayanokōji calls the timing too soon)<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry. I invited you out to eat and made it all about me. Well, let’s eat, shall we?”<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Notices Karuizawa approaching and shoots Ayanokōji a nonplussed look before the girls close ranks.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Wants her friendship first, then a working relationship, and lacks the confidence to ask her directly.<span class=\"pg\">p.17–19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> She arrives with her girls and takes the table back.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: he pulls Ayanokōji to lunch<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p52-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4: the wake-up and the scattered explanations<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p19-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ike-kanji","q":"ch 2  2 0  a hypothetical at the deck restaurant named once  hypothetically   what he and yamauchi would have done at the deck restaurant","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p19-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html#sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p19-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: a hypothetical at the deck restaurant<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.19<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once, hypothetically — what he and Yamauchi would have done at the deck restaurant.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji’s aside: had they been there, they would have “foregone the food and feasted their eyes on the girls instead.”<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p43-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: a passing mention in the comprehension sketch<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p19-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"ch 2  2 0  a hypothetical at the deck restaurant named once  hypothetically   what he and ike would have done at the deck restaurant","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p19-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html#sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p19-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: a hypothetical at the deck restaurant<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.19<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once, hypothetically — what he and Ike would have done at the deck restaurant.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji’s aside: had they been there, they would have “foregone the food and feasted their eyes on the girls instead.”<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p103-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.3: the neck-grab and the camera stimulus<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p20-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei","q":"ch 2  2 0  she reclaims the table crash of the deck lunch  she arrives with her girls and reclaims hirata from the table ayanokoji just fled   ah  so you re here after all  hirata kun  let s eat lunch together","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p20-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p20-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: she reclaims the table<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.20<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Crash of the deck lunch: she arrives with her girls and reclaims Hirata from the table Ayanokōji just fled.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Ah, so you’re here after all, Hirata-kun. Let’s eat lunch together!”<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> The girls pull chairs from another table, push Ayanokōji away, and circle Hirata — peaceful to noisy in seconds.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Happy and carefree in tone while overriding the cancellation; monopolising him is her default.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Takes the lunch he cancelled as if it were never made.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p10-1\">← Before: Ch.1: Karuizawa Kei’s Soliloquy<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p33-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the fourth seat of the zodiac group<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p21-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 1  the koenji corridor and sakura s call corridor on the third deck  koenji dripping from the pool  the bellhop s fourth warning  and ayanokoji s escape route   do you want something from me","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p21-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p21-1\">Ch.2 §2.1: the Kōenji corridor and Sakura’s call<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.21–25<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Corridor on the third deck: Kōenji dripping from the pool, the bellhop’s fourth warning, and Ayanokōji’s escape route.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Do you want something from me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Throws the bellhop’s warning back at Kōenji — “I passed the ball, if you will” — to engineer his own escape.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reads the ship’s signboard map and fixes the layout in his head: nine decks plus a roof, guys on the third deck and girls on the fourth, the 24-hour lounge on the first.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes Sakura’s email call rather than kill time alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p12-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: the cabin reverie and the Horikita bridge<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p26-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.2: Sakura’s worry, Kushida’s interrupt, the school message<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p21-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kouenji-rokusuke","q":"ch 2  2 1  the wet corridor and the signature corridor by the pool  dripping wet in a bathing suit  a fourth warning from the bellhop  a signature demanded   ha ha ha  it appears you ve found me  eh   i don t dry myself off with a towel on principle ever since reaching the age of reason   do you have a pen and paper on hand   even though it s written on such a cheap notepad  it will certainly hold tremendous value in the future   please don t look so suspicious  i am the man who will carry japan s future on his back   oh ho  why  if it isn t little ayanokouji  hmm  what a coincidence   no  no  i ve no real business with you  i ve simply acknowledged you because we are schoolmates  also  though we are certainly not alike in terms of position  you are my roommate","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p21-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html#sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p21-1\">Ch.2 §2.1: the wet corridor and the signature<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.21–24<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Corridor by the pool: dripping wet in a bathing suit, a fourth warning from the bellhop, a signature demanded.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “Ha ha ha! It appears you’ve found me, eh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “I don’t dry myself off with a towel on principle ever since reaching the age of reason.”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “Do you have a pen and paper on hand?”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Signs the bellhop’s notepad “Kouenji Rokusuke” and presents it as a future-valuable gift.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even though it’s written on such a cheap notepad, it will certainly hold tremendous value in the future.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Please don’t look so suspicious. I am the man who will carry Japan’s future on his back.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Repeat offender — this is the fourth hallway stop; believes his autograph outranks the notepad and pen.<span class=\"pg\">p.21–22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narrator’s standing assessment: “Kouenji was like poison.” Classmates steer clear; even Hirata would be brushed off.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Flips his wet hair into Ayanokōji’s face without noticing.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh ho? Why, if it isn’t little Ayanokouji, hmm? What a coincidence.”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, no, I’ve no real business with you. I’ve simply acknowledged you because we are schoolmates. Also, though we are certainly not alike in terms of position, you are my roommate.”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “little Ayanokouji”; confirms the cabin roommate pairing and splashes him mid-sentence.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p52-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4: absent from the room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p25-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou shinohara-satsuki ichihashi-ruri maezono ayanokouji-kiyotaka sakura-airi","q":"ch 2  2 2  the roommate appeal emails ayanokoji to the second deck and stammers through her roommate worry  flees when kushida appears   wah  a ayanokouji kun   n no  no  i m just kind of strangely nervous is all   ayanokouji kun  you re roommates with hirata kun  kouenji kun  and yukimura kun  right   oh  well  to tell you the truth  i i m a little worried about the people i m sharing a room with   i m not sure  i have mixed feelings  i do want to get along with them  but i also want to be alone  too  i m just hopeless  aren t i   oh  didn t i tell you  shinohara san  ichihashi san  and maezono san   i just thought any advice from you  ayanokouji kun  would be good   i i m sorry to just come to you for help like this out of the blue  you re so busy  ayanokouji kun","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p25-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p25-1\">Ch.2 §2.2: the roommate appeal<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.25–28<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Emails Ayanokōji to the second deck and stammers through her roommate worry; flees when Kushida appears.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#ichihashi-ruri\">Ichihashi Ruri<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#maezono\">Maezono<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “Wah! A-Ayanokouji-kun?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “N-no, no. I’m just kind of strangely nervous is all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “Ayanokouji-kun, you’re roommates with Hirata-kun, Kouenji-kun, and Yukimura-kun. Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Nervous to the point of jolt-like surprise; her normally hunched posture straightens at once.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh. Well, to tell you the truth, I…I’m a little worried about the people I’m sharing a room with.”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not sure. I have mixed feelings. I do want to get along with them, but I also want to be alone, too. I’m just hopeless, aren’t I?”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh. Didn’t I tell you? Shinohara-san, Ichihashi-san, and Maezono-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I…just thought any advice from you, Ayanokouji-kun, would be good?”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I-I’m sorry to just come to you for help like this out of the blue. You’re so busy, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> “retreated as fast as her legs would carry her” at Kushida’s arrival.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Rejection and flight; Kushida’s brightness lands as threat.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> Names her as roommate one; the narration adds Shinohara won’t go out of her way for her.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichihashi Ruri<\/b> Roommate two — named only; no file yet (first appearance volume).<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Maezono<\/b> Roommate three — named only; no file yet.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Comes to him because “any advice from you…would be good.”<span class=\"pg\">p.25–28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p97-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.2: the bow stress-talk<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p26-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 2  sakura s worry  kushida s interrupt  the school message second deck hallway  sakura s roommate appeal  kushida s interruption  the school s test message  and the chat with horikita   you re worried because even though you want to get along with them  you don t think you can   it s no big deal  i don t mind it when you come to me for advice  whether i ll be of much help is another story   i m joking  don t you know by now that i m not the sort of person who joins in on stuff   did you get a message from the school just now   chat line  the corpus prints it bare after  i typed   yeah  i did   untagged chat reply  the thread has only these two   my designated meeting time is 18 00  what about yours   chat   mine says 20 40  that seems like a pretty big difference   untagged chat reply   because your time is earlier  i look forward to hearing your report   untagged chat reply  the narration marks her replies instant   understood   chat","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p26-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p26-1\">Ch.2 §2.2: Sakura’s worry, Kushida’s interrupt, the school message<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.26–31<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Second-deck hallway: Sakura’s roommate appeal, Kushida’s interruption, the school’s test message, and the chat with Horikita.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “You’re worried because even though you want to get along with them, you don’t think you can?”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “It’s no big deal. I don’t mind it when you come to me for advice. Whether I’ll be of much help is another story.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I’m joking. Don’t you know by now that I’m not the sort of person who joins in on stuff?”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Ship cabin roommates: Hirata, Kōenji, and Yukimura — Sakura states it; he doesn’t dispute it.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Compares messages with Kushida: his call is 18:00, hers 20:40, her room two doors down from his.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you get a message from the school just now?” (chat line; the corpus prints it bare after “I typed.”)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. I did.” (untagged chat reply; the thread has only these two)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My designated meeting time is 18:00. What about yours?” (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Mine says 20:40. That seems like a pretty big difference.” (untagged chat reply)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because your time is earlier, I look forward to hearing your report.” (untagged chat reply; the narration marks her replies instant)<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Understood.” (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes Horikita’s instant replies as unusual — she normally waits half a day, sometimes days, to read.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Keeps the Horikita chat to himself when Kushida draws near, deciding to wait and see.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Refuses her Class C outing, lets her see the phone, shares nothing about the chat.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Receives her roommate appeal; can only offer limited help.<span class=\"pg\">p.25–28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p21-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1: the Kōenji corridor and Sakura’s call<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p32-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the zodiac briefing opens<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p27-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 2  2 2  the hallway interrupt and the message compare exits a second deck room into the hallway mid meeting plan  interrupts sakura s appeal  then compares school messages with ayanokoji   huh  ayanokouji kun and sakura san  what are you doing here   ah  did i interrupt  i didn t mean to  i was supposed to meet up with some friends   i ve made plans to go see some girls from class c today  do you want to come  ayanokouji kun   oh jeez  come on  you surprised me a little  ayanokouji kun  you re funny","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p27-1\">Ch.2 §2.2: the hallway interrupt and the message compare<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.27–31<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Exits a second-deck room into the hallway mid-meeting-plan; interrupts Sakura’s appeal, then compares school messages with Ayanokōji.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Huh? Ayanokouji-kun and Sakura-san? What are you doing here?”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Ah, did I interrupt? I didn’t mean to. I was supposed to meet up with some friends.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “I’ve made plans to go see some girls from Class C today. Do you want to come, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh jeez, come on. You surprised me a little. Ayanokouji-kun, you’re funny.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Her true self “seemed puzzled by my response” when he says yes — the mask slips a little before the smooth recovery.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Without hesitation shows him her message: 20:40, a room two doors from his.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Draws nearer, curious about his chat with Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> The bright entrance that sends Sakura fleeing; Kushida apologises to no evident purpose.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Invites, reads his joke, shares her phone, watches his screen.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p60-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.5: the puzzled arrival<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v4-p27-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"sakura-airi shinohara-satsuki","q":"ch 2  2 2  named as sakura s roommate named as sakura s first roommate  with the narration s character sketch","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v4-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html#sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v4-p27-1\">Ch.2 §2.2: named as Sakura’s roommate<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.27<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as Sakura’s first roommate, with the narration’s character sketch.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Roommate; the narration sizes her up — close with Karuizawa, “like her boss, really” — reliable and unafraid of a fight, but relentless against people she doesn’t like, so she “probably wouldn’t go out of her way to befriend her.”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p30-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"ch 2  2 2  the message chat chat only  ayanokoji messages her about the school s test notice  she replies instantly   yeah  i did   chat reply  the translation leaves the thread s lines untagged   mine says 20 40  that seems like a pretty big difference   chat   because your time is earlier  i look forward to hearing your report   chat","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p30-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p30-1\">Ch.2 §2.2: the message chat<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.30–31<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chat only: Ayanokōji messages her about the school’s test notice; she replies instantly.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Yeah. I did.” (chat reply; the translation leaves the thread’s lines untagged)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Mine says 20:40. That seems like a pretty big difference.” (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Because your time is earlier, I look forward to hearing your report.” (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Replies instantly — against her usual half-day, sometimes days, reading lag.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Two further chat lines sit unassigned in the translation: “I’m curious about the difference in start times…” and “We can’t know anything for sure at this point.” The volume attribution list keeps them.<span class=\"pg\">p.30–31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Off-page: Hirata’s whole lunch ask is about winning her over, routed through Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.17–19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The chat partner with the earlier slot; she defers his report.<span class=\"pg\">p.30–31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p51-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.5: the Katsuragi warning and the cold exit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p32-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action","w":"sotomura-hideo yukimura-teruhiko mashima-tomonari karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 3  the zodiac briefing opens room 204 on the second deck  mashima s briefing table  sotomura and yukimura already seated  karuizawa as the late fourth","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p32-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p32-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the zodiac briefing opens<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.32–36<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Room 204 on the second deck: Mashima’s briefing table, Sotomura and Yukimura already seated, Karuizawa as the late fourth.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Takes the vacant seat beside Yukimura and waits out the unseen fourth member.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads the setup as ominous — small groups, private rooms, a teacher who won’t take questions: “There was a storm coming, the curtain rising on a new test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> Classmate at the table; the Professor greets him with “Ayanokouji-dono.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The roommate beside him; he stays quiet while Yukimura and Karuizawa trade blows.<span class=\"pg\">p.32, 36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> The briefer: cold, unanswerable, “impossible to read.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32–36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The fourth member; she moves her chair away from him.<span class=\"pg\">p.33–36<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p26-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: Sakura’s worry, Kushida’s interrupt, the school message<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p37-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the four outcomes and the traitor rules<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p32-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae karuizawa-kei mashima-tomonari","q":"ch 2  2 3  the zodiac briefing briefs the four class d students in room 204  zodiac groups  thinking tested four ways   what are you doing  hurry and take a seat   we are still waiting on one more  please sit quietly   i believe you were told punctuality was key  and yet you re late  hurry and take your seat   sotomura  yukimura  ayanokouji  and karuizawa  from class d  without further ado  i will now explain the special test   i will not answer any questions at this time  be quiet and listen   in this special test  all the first year students will be divided into twelve groups based on the signs of the zodiac   society needs three fundamental qualities in order to progress  action  thinking  and teamwork  those with the necessary qualities will become wonderful adults   i ve already told you  i will not be answering any questions   you four gathered here will be in the same group  at this very moment  students in other rooms are receiving the same explanation you are   calm down  you two  yukimura  your concerns are groundless  the test hasn t yet begun  so you won t be affected  besides  your attitude has no bearing on this test","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p32-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html#sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p32-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the zodiac briefing<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.32–36<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Briefs the four Class D students in Room 204: zodiac groups, thinking tested four ways.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “What are you doing? Hurry and take a seat.”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “We are still waiting on one more. Please sit quietly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “I believe you were told punctuality was key, and yet you’re late. Hurry and take your seat”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sotomura, Yukimura, Ayanokouji, and Karuizawa, from Class D. Without further ado, I will now explain the special test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I will not answer any questions at this time. Be quiet and listen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In this special test, all the first-year students will be divided into twelve groups based on the signs of the Zodiac.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Names the four tested abilities: processing information, analyzing the situation, solving after clarifying, and creating new values through imagination.<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Society needs three fundamental qualities in order to progress: action, thinking, and teamwork. Those with the necessary qualities will become wonderful adults.”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve already told you. I will not be answering any questions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You four gathered here will be in the same group. At this very moment, students in other rooms are receiving the same explanation you are.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Calm down, you two. Yukimura, your concerns are groundless. The test hasn’t yet begun, so you won’t be affected. Besides, your attitude has no bearing on this test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Cold and unanswerable; the narrator pits him against Chabashira — she “unmotivated and unnaturally uncooperative,” he “impossible to read.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32–36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> The comparison the narrator draws between the two homeroom instructors.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Warns her twice before shutting her questions down.<span class=\"pg\">p.34–35<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p37-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the handout and the four outcomes<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p32-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko sotomura-hideo","q":"ch 2  2 3  the professor at the briefing table already seated in room 204 beside yukimura when ayanokoji arrives for the zodiac briefing   so  one of the remaining two spots belongs to ayanokouji dono  i see  most agreeable","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p32-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html#sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p32-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the Professor at the briefing table<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.32–36<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Already seated in Room 204 beside Yukimura when Ayanokōji arrives for the zodiac briefing.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “So, one of the remaining two spots belongs to Ayanokouji-dono, I see! Most agreeable!”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Introduced as “The Professor”: overweight first-year in glasses, the male-otaku stereotype, deep in history and machinery — though his speech and inflection come off unintelligible, he somehow communicates.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Silent through the whole briefing and the Karuizawa–Yukimura quarrel; “The Professor and I stayed quiet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.35–36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Greets him with the nerdy “Ayanokouji-dono.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The unexpected pairing — the narrator notes the Professor and Yukimura don’t normally sit together.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p37-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the Professor’s interjections<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p32-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei sotomura-hideo yukimura-teruhiko","q":"ch 2  2 3  odd company  first quarrel seated at mashima s table with the professor  first to spot that the gathering is odd   this is rather odd  isn t it  ayanokouji   how about you shut up and try listening  the test is probably going to start soon  if they dock our points because you keep blabbing  are you gonna take responsibility   even back on the deserted island  you dragged us all down  can you try not to cause any more problems","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p32-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p32-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: odd company, first quarrel<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.32, p.36<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Seated at Mashima’s table with the Professor; first to spot that the gathering is odd.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “This is rather odd, isn’t it? Ayanokouji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “How about you shut up and try listening? The test is probably going to start soon. If they dock our points because you keep blabbing, are you gonna take responsibility?”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Even back on the deserted island, you dragged us all down. Can you try not to cause any more problems?”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> First to lose patience with Karuizawa; point-anxious and practical.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Trades insults with her under the teacher’s eye.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> Paired oddly at the table, by the narrator’s note.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p37-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the quarrel at the table<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p33-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko mashima-tomonari hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei","q":"ch 2  2 3  the fourth seat of the zodiac group fourth seat of the class d zodiac group  arrives to find three boys and a teacher  and questions it immediately   huh  what s going on  why are yukimura kun and these other guys here   w wait a minute  i don t understand  what do you mean  explain a test  the test was already over  right  also  what s the deal with these guys  this is really weird   jeez  all right  fine  i ll shut up   what do you mean by  test our thinking   i don t get what any of this means  can you explain it in a way that s easier to understand   these guys gross me out  why am i on a team together with boys  honestly  i hate it though being with hirata kun would be fine   huh  when and how exactly did i cause problems  you re pissing me off","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p33-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p33-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the fourth seat of the zodiac group<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.33–36<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Fourth seat of the Class D zodiac group; arrives to find three boys and a teacher, and questions it immediately.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Huh? What’s going on? Why are Yukimura-kun and these other guys here?”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “W-wait a minute. I don’t understand. What do you mean, explain a test? The test was already over, right? Also, what’s the deal with these guys? This is really weird.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Jeez, all right. Fine, I’ll shut up.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Studies the three boys, then lifts her chair and moves it away from Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What do you mean by ‘test our thinking’?”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t get what any of this means. Can you explain it in a way that’s easier to understand?”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “These guys gross me out. Why am I on a team together with boys? Honestly, I hate it…though being with Hirata-kun would be fine.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? When and how exactly did I cause problems? You’re pissing me off.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Barrages the teacher until told to be quiet twice; complies unhappily; blunt about the boys.<span class=\"pg\">p.33–36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> His “you dragged us all down” lands; she fires back that he’s pissing her off.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> Defies the cold briefer, then submits.<span class=\"pg\">p.33–35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The only boy on the team she’ll tolerate.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p20-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: she reclaims the table<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p37-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the interrupter, the werewolf, the phone call<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p37-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"inner spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei mashima-tomonari ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 3  the four outcomes and the traitor rules still at mashima s table  the group roster  the handout of four outcomes  and the werewolf detour  all read through ayanokoji s eyes   karuizawa  if you don t change your attitude toward the teachers  it might leave a mark on your permanent record  that wouldn t be good  right  reads the traitor rules as flipping the test on its head  with answers accepted any time  no one would seriously aim for outcome  1  reduces the exam to four possibilities   the honest outcome  1  a wrong guess at the end  the traitor finding the vip  and the traitor misled   and wants to avoid the last one most of all","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p37-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p37-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the four outcomes and the traitor rules<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.37–49<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Still at Mashima’s table: the group roster, the handout of four outcomes, and the Werewolf detour, all read through Ayanokōji’s eyes.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Karuizawa, if you don’t change your attitude toward the teachers, it might leave a mark on your permanent record. That wouldn’t be good, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Reads the traitor rules as flipping the test on its head: with answers accepted any time, no one would seriously aim for Outcome #1.<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Reduces the exam to four possibilities — the honest Outcome #1, a wrong guess at the end, the traitor finding the VIP, and the traitor misled — and wants to avoid the last one most of all.<span class=\"pg\">p.47–48<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Depressed hearing Karuizawa rank the three of them below Hirata, though he tries not to care.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Knows Ichinose from Class B and Ibuki from Class C off the printed roster; of Ibuki he thinks being in the same group “was a perverse kind of fate.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Has never heard of the party game Werewolf — Karuizawa’s amazement lands on genuine ignorance.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Easily memorizes the prohibited-actions list: phone theft, threats for VIP information, impersonation by borrowed phone, and cross-class discussion until the exam ends — each punishable up to expulsion.<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes the school’s anonymity design means any school-sent message is “100% the truth.”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Warns her about her permanent record; she brushes it off.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> The briefer he watches absorb Karuizawa’s interruptions without expression.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p32-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the zodiac briefing opens<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p50-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the hallway split<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p37-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko mashima-tomonari sotomura-hideo hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei","q":"ch 2  2 3  the interrupter  the werewolf  the phone call through the briefing she trades smirks with yukimura  interrupts mashima repeatedly  learns the four outcomes  and finally phones hirata   hmph   after ayanokoji s warning about her permanent record   ugh  jeez  this sucks  i can t deal with these three  hirata kun would have been so much better   gross  even if there were a hundred or two hundred of you  you still wouldn t be worth a single hair on hirata kun s head   to the professor   ugh  well  at any rate  i ll just report it to hirata kun later   okay  okay  i understand that we re being divided into these groups  but why is it only the four of us getting this explanation  i thought you d explain things after our entire group was gathered together   w wait a minute  what do you mean  i still don t get it at all  we re going to be grouped with students from other classes  isn t that crazy  though  aren t the other classes supposed to be the enemy   jeez  everyone s gonna be jealous of the vip  not being picked for it would be unfair  no matter what happens  that person still gets points  and if we get outcome  1  it s a million points   wait a second  ayanokouji kun  don t tell me you don t know about werewolf  whoa  i can t believe it   i m sorry  it s just  like  not having friends must be so sad   when his ignorance shows   well  you get together with your friends  and then you divide people up as either villagers or wolves  the one who survives at the end is th","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p37-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p37-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the interrupter, the werewolf, the phone call<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.37–50<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Through the briefing she trades smirks with Yukimura, interrupts Mashima repeatedly, learns the four outcomes, and finally phones Hirata.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Hmph.” (after Ayanokōji’s warning about her permanent record)<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Ugh, jeez! This sucks! I can’t deal with these three! Hirata-kun would have been so much better!”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Gross. Even if there were a hundred or two hundred of you, you still wouldn’t be worth a single hair on Hirata-kun’s head.” (to the Professor)<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ugh. Well, at any rate, I’ll just report it to Hirata-kun later.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay, okay. I understand that we’re being divided into these groups, but why is it only the four of us getting this explanation? I thought you’d explain things after our entire group was gathered together.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “W-wait a minute. What do you mean? I still don’t get it at all. We’re going to be grouped with students from other classes? Isn’t that crazy, though? Aren’t the other classes supposed to be the enemy?”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Jeez, everyone’s gonna be jealous of the VIP! Not being picked for it would be unfair! No matter what happens, that person still gets points! And if we get Outcome #1, it’s a million points!”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Half-listens so hard her comprehension goes “abnormally bad” — the narration contrasts her with Sudō and Ike, who score poorly, versus her refusal to listen.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait a second. Ayanokouji-kun, don’t tell me you don’t know about Werewolf? Whoa, I can’t believe it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry. It’s just, like, not having friends must be so sad.” (when his ignorance shows)<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, you get together with your friends, and then you divide people up as either villagers or wolves. The one who survives at the end is the winner. Get it?” (explaining Werewolf)<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And that’s…on the other side of the handout, right? Is it okay if we turn it over?”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Umm, umm. I kind of get it, but I kind of don’t.”<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, we can’t leave the room? How long do we need to stay in there?”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Agh. Well, this sounds kinda annoying, but I guess I do understand somewhat. Ugh. I just wish we had a test that was more fun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Ignores Yukimura’s huddle pitch, takes out her phone mid-hallway, and calls Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, hi, Hirata-kun? There was something I wanted to talk to you about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Trades barbs with him from the first smirks to the hallway dismissal.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> Interrupts him four times; he answers without expression.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> The “hundred or two hundred of you” line lands on the Professor.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The call she makes the moment the briefing ends.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p33-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the fourth seat of the zodiac group<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p80-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: the Rabbit votes and Manabe’s phone<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p37-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei yukimura-teruhiko mashima-tomonari","q":"ch 2  2 3  the handout and the four outcomes carries the briefing to its end  cross class groups  the printed roster  the vip handout  werewolf  and the meeting logistics   listen  your group assignments are a done deal  you cannot change them  to gain a good result on the test  you must get along   finished  please let me continue my explanation   it would appear that you cannot help but be concerned by this small gathering  therefore  i will try to provide an answer  this is neither a conspiracy against the students  nor is it harassment  it s rather simple  the groups don t consist of members from just one class  they are made up of about three to five individuals collected from each class  if we didn t explain things in advance  we would run the risk of confusion   you ve been competing until now  your school lives have only just begun  you shouldn t run around like a chicken with its head cut off this early  yukimura   right now  you shouldn t spend your energy on trying to understand this test  rather  focus on how to think  your group assignment is  rabbit  here is a list of the members  you will be required to return this list when you leave the room  if you feel it s necessary  i would recommend trying to memorize it now   don t worry  i will answer any questions you have  i believe you will be able to understand everything afterward  probably   the point of this test is to ignore the prior fraught relationships between classes a through d  if you do  you ll have a s","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p37-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html#sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p37-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the handout and the four outcomes<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.37–49<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Carries the briefing to its end: cross-class groups, the printed roster, the VIP handout, Werewolf, and the meeting logistics.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “Listen. Your group assignments are a done deal. You cannot change them. To gain a good result on the test, you must get along.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “Finished? Please let me continue my explanation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “It would appear that you cannot help but be concerned by this small gathering. Therefore, I will try to provide an answer. This is neither a conspiracy against the students, nor is it harassment. It’s rather simple. The groups…”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>26 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It would appear that you cannot help but be concerned by this small gathering. Therefore, I will try to provide an answer. This is neither a conspiracy against the students, nor is it harassment. It’s rather simple. The groups don’t consist of members from just one class; they are made up of about three to five individuals collected from each class. If we didn’t explain things in advance, we would run the risk of confusion.”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ve been competing until now? Your school lives have only just begun. You shouldn’t run around like a chicken with its head cut off this early, Yukimura.”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Right now, you shouldn’t spend your energy on trying to understand this test. Rather, focus on how to think. Your group assignment is ‘Rabbit’. Here is a list of the members. You will be required to return this list when you leave the room. If you feel it’s necessary, I would recommend trying to memorize it now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t worry. I will answer any questions you have. I believe you will be able to understand everything afterward. Probably.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The point of this test is to ignore the prior fraught relationships between Classes A through D. If you do, you’ll have a shortcut.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “From this point on, you are no longer acting as members of Class D, but rather as members of the Rabbit group. Whether you pass or fail this test depends on each group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Four outcomes only; handouts of the grade items may be verified on the spot but not taken, photographed, or copied.<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The test runs from 8:00 a.m. day one’s message to 9:00 p.m. day four; two one-hour group meetings daily at set times and rooms; answers accepted only 9:30–10:00 p.m. the final night, by email, first submission per group counts, one answer per student, VIPs may not submit, results emailed 11:00 p.m.<span class=\"pg\">p.40–41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Outcome #1: a correct final answer pays every group member 500,000 private points. Outcome #2: no or wrong final submission pays only the VIP 500,000.<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This exam has one critical element. Understand it, and this test will not pose a problem. The key element is the existence of the VIP. There is only one VIP in the group. In this test, you’re after the name of the VIP. It’s that simple. For example, Yukimura, let’s say that you were chosen as VIP. The correct answer for the Rabbit group would be ‘Yukimura.’”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Now then, as for Outcome #2… In the event that the VIP’s identity is not discovered before the end of the examination, and no one in your group found out the identity of the VIP or some even attempted to lie about the identity, then only the VIP will be awarded points, just as it says. He or she will receive 500,000 points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you understand the explanation for the first two? If you do not, then we cannot continue.”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Regarding the remaining outcomes, they are written on the reverse side of the handout. However, please wait a bit before turning the paper over.”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Very well, I will explain in simpler terms. Have you played the game Werewolf?”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although I said that there is only one VIP in the group, if the VIP is exposed right away, then Outcomes #3 and #4 will appear.”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Outcome #3: an early correct answer by a non-VIP pays that student 500,000 private points and their class 50 class points, costs the VIP’s class 50, and ends the group’s test — a VIP-classmate’s early correct answer doesn’t count. Outcome #4: an early wrong answer by a non-VIP costs their class 50 class points and pays the VIP 500,000 plus 50 to the VIP’s class — a VIP-classmate’s early wrong answer doesn’t count.<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The school will take anonymity into account during this test. At the end, only the outcomes for each group and the increase or decrease in points for each class will be announced. In other words, we will not announce the names of the VIPs or those who submitted answers. Also, if you wish, you may have a temporary ID assigned to you, to which you can transfer points. It is also possible to divide points up and receive them that way. If you yourself remain quiet, there should be no fear of discovery after the test. Of course, if it’s not necessary for you to hide your identity, you may receive your points openly. That is perfectly fine.”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Outcomes #3 and #4 are very different from the first two. That’s why they are listed on the reverse side of the sheet. With that, the explanation is complete.”<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There should also be a list of prohibited actions on the sheet. Make sure to examine it thoroughly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Prohibited: stealing phones, threats to confirm VIP information, using another’s phone to submit — up to expulsion; cross-class discussion until the exam ends — expulsion; school messages may not be copied, deleted, transferred, or modified.<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Tomorrow, you will go to your designated room at 1:00 p.m. and again at 8:00 p.m. Your group’s name will be displayed on a nameplate… Be sure to introduce yourselves when you meet the other members for the first time. After you’ve entered, leaving the room during the examination is not permitted. Please use the restroom ahead of time. In the event that you feel ill or can’t endure it any longer, please contact your homeroom teacher immediately and make a request.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49-50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The explanation is written on the sheet. The discussion period is for one hour. Aside from self-introduction upon your initial meeting, you are free to use that time however you like. Once the hour has passed, you are free to remain in the room or to leave.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The school is committed to fairness, so we will be strict and impartial. After the VIP has been selected, we will not accept any changes, not even if the VIP wants to be changed. In addition, copying, deleting, transferring, or modifying emails sent from the school is prohibited. Understand these points clearly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Flat, unchanging tone throughout; sharp-eyed when they reach for the paper — “It seemed like the exam had already begun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41–43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Absorbs her four interruptions without expression.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Cuts his chicken-with-its-head-short speech down.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p32-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the zodiac briefing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p67-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the phrasing he still hears<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p37-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko karuizawa-kei sotomura-hideo","q":"ch 2  2 3  the professor s interjections three appearances inside the briefing day  the three heads quip  the confused handout  and the anime powered exit   heh  but you know  three heads are better than one  thus  if the three of us join together  we might be able to surpass the good hirata dono  my dear lady   this has turned into quite a bothersome ordeal  being partnered with a bitch like that  i mean   after karuizawa s call   that is certainly true  hmm  she s an unforgivable bitch  she s a bitch among bitches  wouldn t you say   agreeing with yukimura   i am terribly sorry  but i must decline your invitation  for you see  the love love alive anime calls  and i cannot afford to miss its siren song  i bid you farewell  hi ya","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p37-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html#sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p37-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the Professor’s interjections<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.37, p.41, p.51<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Three appearances inside the briefing day: the three-heads quip, the confused handout, and the anime-powered exit.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “Heh. But you know, three heads are better than one. Thus, if the three of us join together, we might be able to surpass the good Hirata-dono, my dear lady,”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “This has turned into quite a bothersome ordeal. Being partnered with a bitch like that, I mean,” (after Karuizawa’s call)<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “That is certainly true, hmm? She’s an unforgivable bitch. She’s a bitch among bitches, wouldn’t you say?” (agreeing with Yukimura)<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Cocked his head over the handout alongside Karuizawa, “as if wracking their brains.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I am terribly sorry, but I must decline your invitation. For you see, the Love Love Alive anime calls, and I cannot afford to miss its siren song. I bid you farewell. Hi-ya!”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narration notes he often claims he wants the 2D world and that 2D women are perfect — which is why real girls like Karuizawa are rejected outright.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Echoes his exact “space cadets” line from minutes earlier, then turns down his huddle for anime.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Mocks her with the three-heads line, then insults her out of earshot.<span class=\"pg\">p.37, 51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p32-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the Professor at the briefing table<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p78-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: the Professor in Rabbit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p37-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei mashima-tomonari yukimura-teruhiko","q":"ch 2  2 3  the quarrel at the table spends the briefing trading barbs with karuizawa and absorbing mashima s rebuke   i  p pardon me   after mashima cuts him off   karuizawa  please  i m begging you  shut up and listen  i can t concentrate when you prattle on   you two are idiots  i ll explain it later  so don t keep bothering mashima sensei   shooting down karuizawa and the professor","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p37-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p37-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the quarrel at the table<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.37–46<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Spends the briefing trading barbs with Karuizawa and absorbing Mashima’s rebuke.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “I… P-pardon me.” (after Mashima cuts him off)<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Karuizawa, please. I’m begging you, shut up and listen. I can’t concentrate when you prattle on”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “You two are idiots. I’ll explain it later, so don’t keep bothering Mashima-sensei.” (shooting down Karuizawa and the Professor)<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Snorted derisively at Karuizawa without saying a word.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “seemed like he wanted to cozy up to school officials” — the narration’s read on why he polices the others’ questions.<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The main target of his exasperation.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> The teacher he stammers an apology to.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p32-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: odd company, first quarrel<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p49-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the failed huddle<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p39-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"kanzaki-ryuuji ichinose-honami","q":"ch 2  named on the rabbit roster twice named without a scene  on the printed rabbit group roster  and in kanzaki s portrait of a trusted class b boy","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p39-1\">Ch.2: named on the Rabbit roster<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.39, p.56<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Twice named without a scene: on the printed Rabbit group roster, and in Kanzaki’s portrait of a trusted Class B boy.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Listed among the three Class B members of the Rabbit group — Ayanokōji knows her by name off the sheet.<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Kanzaki is described as the Class B student whom “Ichinose—Class B’s leader—seemed to trust.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Her trust is the credential the narration gives him.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p81-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: taking the lead in Rabbit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p43-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ike-kanji","q":"ch 2  2 3  a passing mention in the comprehension sketch named once as a contrast while the narration sizes up karuizawa s refusal to listen","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p43-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html#sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p43-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: a passing mention in the comprehension sketch<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.43<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once as a contrast while the narration sizes up Karuizawa’s refusal to listen.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The comparison: her problem “wasn’t that she scored poorly on tests like Sudou or Ike” — unlike them, she simply won’t listen.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v4-p19-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: a hypothetical at the deck restaurant<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p43-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"sudou-ken","q":"ch 2  2 3  a passing mention in the comprehension sketch named once as a contrast while the narration sizes up karuizawa s refusal to listen","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p43-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p43-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: a passing mention in the comprehension sketch<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.43<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once as a contrast while the narration sizes up Karuizawa’s refusal to listen.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The comparison: her problem “wasn’t that she scored poorly on tests like Sudou or Ike” — unlike them, she simply won’t listen.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v4-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: a passing mention in Hirata’s inventory<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p49-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei sotomura-hideo ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko","q":"ch 2  2 3  the failed huddle in the room and then the hallway  he probes ayanokoji  pitches a three man plan  and watches it dissolve   hey  ayanokouji  you ve been quiet  do you actually understand everything   for crying out loud  why on earth was i lumped in with a bunch of space cadets   said once in the room   why on earth was i lumped in with a bunch of space cadets   repeated in the hallway  word for word   i hate to say this  but if we have to be in the same group  we need to put up a unified front  a lot of things will depend on who the vip is  but for now  the four of us should discuss things   h hey  karuizawa  are you listening   maybe in the morning there ll be a notification that one of us was chosen as the vip  if one of us is chosen  it d be smart not to spread it around carelessly  we don t know who might be listening  let s get to a secure location before sharing info   to be honest  i really hate it  no matter what i do  she ll only drag us down   on karuizawa   karuizawa may be gone  but i want to talk about tomorrow  it makes sense to discuss it with just the three of us  let s go","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p49-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p49-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the failed huddle<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.49–51<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the room and then the hallway: he probes Ayanokōji, pitches a three-man plan, and watches it dissolve.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Hey, Ayanokouji. You’ve been quiet. Do you actually understand everything?”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “For crying out loud, why on earth was I lumped in with a bunch of space cadets?” (said once in the room)<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Why on earth was I lumped in with a bunch of space cadets?” (repeated in the hallway, word for word)<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I hate to say this, but if we have to be in the same group, we need to put up a unified front. A lot of things will depend on who the VIP is, but for now, the four of us should discuss things.”<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “H-hey, Karuizawa. Are you listening?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Maybe in the morning there’ll be a notification that one of us was…chosen as the VIP. If one of us is chosen, it’d be smart not to spread it around carelessly. We don’t know who might be listening. Let’s get to a secure location before sharing info.”<span class=\"pg\">p.50-51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To be honest, I really hate it. No matter what I do, she’ll only drag us down.” (on Karuizawa)<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Karuizawa may be gone, but I want to talk about tomorrow. It makes sense to discuss it with just the three of us. Let’s go.”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sighs and shakes it off when the Professor declines and Ayanokōji doesn’t engage — “He didn’t seem to want to work with me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Her phone call kills the huddle; he vents about her afterward.<span class=\"pg\">p.50–51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> The invitee who bows out for Love Love Alive.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Probes whether he understood the briefing.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p37-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the quarrel at the table<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p52-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4: absent from the room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p50-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 3  the hallway split leaving mashima s room  yukimura s huddle plan collapses when karuizawa calls hirata and the professor declines   for the most part  i guess  i d like you to explain the things i don t fully understand later  though   to yukimura  who asked whether he understood","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p50-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p50-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the hallway split<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.50–51<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Leaving Mashima’s room: Yukimura’s huddle plan collapses when Karuizawa calls Hirata and the Professor declines.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “For the most part, I guess. I’d like you to explain the things I don’t fully understand later, though.” (to Yukimura, who asked whether he understood)<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Feigns incompleteness on purpose — “I wasn’t going to tell Hirata anything more” in the later hallway talk — and lets Yukimura’s discontent pass unnoticed.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Agrees the ship may be bugged, accepts Yukimura’s secure-location plan in principle, then reports the Rabbit rules to Horikita by chat and starts shaping a strategy alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The one classmate who tries to build a three-man huddle with him; Yukimura sighs and drops it.<span class=\"pg\">p.50–51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p37-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the four outcomes and the traitor rules<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p52-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4: the wake-up and the scattered explanations<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p51-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei kanzaki-ryuuji ryuuen-kakeru hirata-yousuke horikita-suzune","q":"ch 2  2 5  the katsuragi warning and the cold exit off screen first   ayanokoji reports the rabbit rules to her by chat   then on the second deck she faces katsuragi  holds against kanzaki s interlude  and turns her back on ryuen   yes  i am  and what exactly does that have to do with you   to katsuragi   you wanted to speak with me  funny  didn t you completely ignore me the other day   that s rather petty  from class a s perspective  are we such a big deal  i mean  there s a significant gap in points between us   you needn t concern yourself  class d has always been regarded as inferior  i d welcome any change in our reputation   what do you mean   when katsuragi calls the island win luck   we haven t gotten into college yet  i don t think you and i are so different  the school arbitrarily divided us into different classes  don t forget that   if we re going to continue this pointless conversation  i d prefer to just go inside  besides  it s about time   flipping her hair away from ryuen","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p51-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p51-1\">Ch.2 §2.5: the Katsuragi warning and the cold exit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.51, p.55–61<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Off-screen first — Ayanokōji reports the Rabbit rules to her by chat — then on the second deck she faces Katsuragi, holds against Kanzaki’s interlude, and turns her back on Ryūen.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Yes, I am. And what exactly does that have to do with you?” (to Katsuragi)<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “You wanted to speak with me? Funny. Didn’t you completely ignore me the other day?”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “That’s rather petty. From Class A’s perspective, are we such a big deal? I mean, there’s a significant gap in points between us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Receives his chat report on the Rabbit group’s rules; her reply is not printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You needn’t concern yourself. Class D has always been regarded as inferior. I’d welcome any change in our reputation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What do you mean?” (when Katsuragi calls the island win luck)<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We haven’t gotten into college yet. I don’t think you and I are so different. The school arbitrarily divided us into different classes. Don’t forget that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If we’re going to continue this pointless conversation, I’d prefer to just go inside. Besides, it’s about time.” (flipping her hair away from Ryūen)<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Doesn’t back down before the Class A entourage; the narration credits her — weak-willed students would ingratiate themselves, she acts as she always does.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads her own new reputation: other classes now treat her selfishness as class concern and fear her as a hidden mastermind.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The pivot from his island-test indifference to a Class A threat.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Declines his rescue — “You needn’t concern yourself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Exits on him mid-provocation.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Both summoned to the 20:40 meeting (see Hirata’s row).<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p30-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: the message chat<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p63-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.0: the Blue Ocean briefing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p52-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"inner spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 4  the wake up and the scattered explanations just before 20 30 he wakes in the third deck cabin to hirata s apology  and they step out together toward the evening s meetings   can t really say  i haven t been thinking about the exam like you  horikita  and yukimura have  i m not smart  either  so i haven t really noticed much   deflecting hirata s request for observations   yeah  i think you re right  hirata  it would definitely be more efficient to explain the test to all the students at the same time  rather than dividing us into groups and doing it in stages  suspects the school s deliberately scattered briefings mean their  thinking  is already being tested","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p52-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p52-1\">Ch.2 §2.4: the wake-up and the scattered explanations<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.52–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Just before 20:30 he wakes in the third-deck cabin to Hirata’s apology, and they step out together toward the evening’s meetings.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Can’t really say. I haven’t been thinking about the exam like you, Horikita, and Yukimura have. I’m not smart, either, so I haven’t really noticed much.” (deflecting Hirata’s request for observations)<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Yeah, I think you’re right, Hirata. It would definitely be more efficient to explain the test to all the students at the same time, rather than dividing us into groups and doing it in stages.”<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Suspects the school’s deliberately scattered briefings mean their “thinking” is already being tested.<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Walks him to the second deck while sharing nothing of substance.<span class=\"pg\">p.52–53<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p50-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the hallway split<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.5: the 20:40 gathering<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p52-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 2  2 4  the wake up and the scattered explanations in the third deck cabin he straightens his luggage  puts on his uniform  and wakes ayanokoji for the evening s meetings   i m sorry  did i wake you   would you like to come with me  i was thinking the school s message should be coming pretty soon   did you notice anything  ayanokouji kun  if it s okay  i d like you to share it with me   well  i was wondering why the explanations are so scattered  i thought maybe the school wanted to avoid the confusion and trouble that would come from explaining things in one large group  but after thinking about it  i don t believe it would take much more effort to announce the rules to everyone at once","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p52-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p52-1\">Ch.2 §2.4: the wake-up and the scattered explanations<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.52–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the third-deck cabin he straightens his luggage, puts on his uniform, and wakes Ayanokōji for the evening’s meetings.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “I’m sorry. Did I wake you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Would you like to come with me? I was thinking the school’s message should be coming pretty soon.”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Did you notice anything, Ayanokouji-kun? If it’s okay, I’d like you to share it with me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Already knows the test’s specifics — Yukimura told him over their meal — and several students have come to talk it through with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I was wondering why the explanations are so…scattered. I thought maybe the school wanted to avoid the confusion and trouble that would come from explaining things in one large group, but after thinking about it, I don’t believe it would take much more effort to announce the rules to everyone at once.”<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Plans to ask a teacher directly about the staged briefings.<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Wakes him, walks him down, gets only a deflection for his troubles.<span class=\"pg\">p.52–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> His inside source on the Rabbit rules.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p17-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: the ask, be the bridge to Horikita<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.5: the 20:40 gathering<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p52-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"kouenji-rokusuke","q":"ch 2  2 4  absent from the room named only as missing  when ayanokoji wakes in the cabin at 20 30  the narration notes the room s other occupants are gone","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p52-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html#sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p52-1\">Ch.2 §2.4: absent from the room<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.52<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named only as missing: when Ayanokōji wakes in the cabin at 20:30, the narration notes the room’s other occupants are gone.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Neither Yukimura nor Kouenji were in the room.” — absent from the third-deck cabin while Hirata straightens his luggage.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p21-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1: the wet corridor and the signature<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p64-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the grade-theory name-check<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p52-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"yukimura-teruhiko","q":"ch 2  2 4  absent from the room named only as missing  when ayanokoji wakes in the cabin  neither he nor koenji is there","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p52-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p52-1\">Ch.2 §2.4: absent from the room<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.52<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named only as missing: when Ayanokōji wakes in the cabin, neither he nor Kōenji is there.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Absent from the third-deck cabin at 20:30 — Ayanokōji notes the room holds only himself and Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p49-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the failed huddle<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p78-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: from the convenient plan to Ichinose<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p54-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune katsuragi-kouhei ryuuen-kakeru kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 5  the 20 40 gathering at the second deck meeting place he watches katsuragi confront horikita  kanzaki intercede  ryuen prowl  and kushida arrive puzzled   who are those people   asking hirata to name the waiting students  notes katsuragi s entourage and horikita s changed standing  other classes now see her as  a puppet master  a mastermind who worked behind the scenes  credits horikita s cold shoulder resilience   the island win is his  but she took the spotlight to keep him hidden  expects a huge showdown between katsuragi and ryuen before the test begins  it doesn t come   well then  good luck   leaving hirata at the gathering","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p54-1\">Ch.2 §2.5: the 20:40 gathering<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.54–61<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the second-deck meeting place he watches Katsuragi confront Horikita, Kanzaki intercede, Ryūen prowl, and Kushida arrive puzzled.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Who are those people?” (asking Hirata to name the waiting students)<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Notes Katsuragi’s entourage and Horikita’s changed standing: other classes now see her as “a puppet master, a mastermind who worked behind the scenes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Well then, good luck.” (leaving Hirata at the gathering)<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Burns Morimiya and Tokitō’s names and faces into memory on Hirata’s tip, then keeps to the line without making a fuss.<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Credits Horikita’s cold-shoulder resilience — the island win is his, but she took the spotlight to keep him hidden.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Expects a huge showdown between Katsuragi and Ryūen before the test begins; it doesn’t come.<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Stands by as Katsuragi threatens her class and Kanzaki pulls him off; impressed she won’t be shaken.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Watches the Class A leader pivot from ignoring Horikita to warning her.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Notes the demented chuckle and the docile lackeys trailing him.<span class=\"pg\">p.57–60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Present when she wanders into the gathering, puzzled.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p52-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.4: the wake-up and the scattered explanations<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p63-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.0: the 8:00 café and the Ryūen interrupt<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p54-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei kanzaki-ryuuji kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 2  2 5  the 20 40 gathering second deck meeting place  he names the waiting students for ayanokoji  then stands inside the katsuragi horikita ryuen current   it doesn t seem like all of these people are in my group   that s morimiya kun  from class a  and that one near the elevator is tokitou kun  from class c   the well connected answer   yes  though if i m with you  kanzaki kun  and katsuragi kun  struggle has to be inevitable   answering kanzaki s sympathy   don t worry  no matter who is in my group  i ll do my best   to katsuragi  positive as always","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p54-1\">Ch.2 §2.5: the 20:40 gathering<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.54–61<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Second-deck meeting place: he names the waiting students for Ayanokōji, then stands inside the Katsuragi–Horikita–Ryūen current.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “It doesn’t seem like all of these people are in my group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “That’s Morimiya-kun, from Class A. And that one near the elevator is Tokitou-kun, from Class C.” (the well-connected answer)<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Yes. Though if I’m with you, Kanzaki-kun, and Katsuragi-kun, struggle has to be inevitable.” (answering Kanzaki’s sympathy)<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t worry. No matter who is in my group, I’ll do my best.” (to Katsuragi, positive as always)<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Positive through the threat display; Kushida reads his steadiness as the sign that the battle will be grueling.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Addressed as the group’s Class A anchor.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> The Class B boy who spots him landed in trouble.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She finds him amid the gathering and takes his composure for reassurance.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Both summoned to the same 20:40 meeting — the team Katsuragi named.<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p52-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.4: the wake-up and the scattered explanations<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p64-1\">→ After: Ch.3: named on the Dragon roster and in the Ichinose comparison<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p54-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kanzaki-ryuuji ryuuen-kakeru hirata-yousuke katsuragi-kouhei","q":"ch 2  2 5  the class a pivot on horikita at the 20 40 gathering he singles horikita out of the line  then holds court against her  kanzaki  and ryuen   unless i m mistaken  you re also in the group meeting at 20 40  yes   that s good news  i wanted to speak with you again  i m also in the 20 40 group  starting tomorrow  we will be working together   you re correct  i certainly haven t acknowledged anyone in class d until now  however  considering the incredible results from the last test  it would be impossible for me not to pay attention to you  wouldn t you agree  you laid the groundwork to win  and succeeded handsomely   i don t know what the future might hold  but should class d overtake class c  know that class a would attack you without mercy   that s certainly true  however  we must be cautious  it s no laughing matter when those who have been perceived as weak and stupid begin to rise up  if one class manages to change its station  we must be vigilant  i would give the same warning to both classes b and c   however  just because you got lucky and won by complete chance doesn t make us equals   anyone could accomplish something like that out of pure luck  it s better that you don t grow arrogant and behave foolishly after a win that came about by chance  remember that the difference in our class points is still massive   that s a rather deplorable thing to say  especially when academic success is the most important factor in determining our futures  you realize that ja","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html#sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p54-1\">Ch.2 §2.5: the Class A pivot on Horikita<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.54–60<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the 20:40 gathering he singles Horikita out of the line, then holds court against her, Kanzaki, and Ryūen.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “Unless I’m mistaken, you’re also in the group meeting at 20:40, yes?”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “That’s good news. I wanted to speak with you again. I’m also in the 20:40 group. Starting tomorrow, we will be working together.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “You’re correct. I certainly haven’t acknowledged anyone in Class D until now. However, considering the incredible results from the last test, it would be impossible for me not to pay attention to you. Wouldn’t you agree? You…”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re correct. I certainly haven’t acknowledged anyone in Class D until now. However, considering the incredible results from the last test, it would be impossible for me not to pay attention to you. Wouldn’t you agree? You laid the groundwork to win, and succeeded handsomely.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know what the future might hold, but…should Class D overtake Class C, know that Class A would attack you without mercy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s certainly true. However, we must be cautious. It’s no laughing matter when those who have been perceived as weak and stupid begin to rise up. If one class manages to change its station, we must be vigilant. I would give the same warning to both Classes B and C.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, just because you got lucky and won by complete chance doesn’t make us equals.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Anyone could accomplish something like that out of pure luck. It’s better that you don’t grow arrogant and behave foolishly after a win that came about by chance. Remember that the difference in our class points is still massive.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s a rather deplorable thing to say. Especially when academic success is the most important factor in determining our futures. You realize that Japan is often referred to as an academic society?” (to Ryūen)<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I won’t let you bring your awful attitude to this test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, it doesn’t matter. Since we’re in the same group now, we’ll be able to talk at length.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you okay, Hirata? I think this is going to be an especially grueling battle.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calm and collected to a degree that reads as college-age; “most had already acknowledged him as their leader” — the Class A entourage glares on cue.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Dismissive gesture “like he was brushing dirt off his clothes” while calling the island win luck.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The pivot from island-test indifference to a formal Class A threat.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Brushed off by him, then trading academic-ability arguments with Ryūen in front of him.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The “Beauty and the Beast” provocation and the awful-attitude standoff.<span class=\"pg\">p.57–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Names him the group’s grinding battle ahead.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p64-1\">→ After: Ch.3: named as the island strategist and the no-discussion plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p56-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune katsuragi-kouhei hirata-yousuke ichinose-honami kanzaki-ryuuji","q":"ch 2  2 5  the class b interlude walks quietly past katsuragi s entourage to pull the heat off horikita  then greets hirata s arrival   i don t much like ganging up on people  or threatening other classes   you don t need to waste time on katsuragi  he s just trying to get to you   to horikita  gentlemanly despite not being on good terms with her   hirata  looks like you landed in a troublesome group   oh  i don t think so   when hirata says struggle with him  kanzaki  and katsuragi is inevitable","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p56-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html#sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p56-1\">Ch.2 §2.5: the Class B interlude<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.56–57<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walks quietly past Katsuragi’s entourage to pull the heat off Horikita, then greets Hirata’s arrival.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “I don’t much like ganging up on people, or threatening other classes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “You don’t need to waste time on Katsuragi. He’s just trying to get to you.” (to Horikita, gentlemanly despite not being on good terms with her)<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “Hirata, looks like you landed in a troublesome group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, I don’t think so.” (when Hirata says struggle with him, Kanzaki, and Katsuragi is inevitable)<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Honest type — long hair without slacker energy; the narration notes Ichinose, Class B’s leader, seems to trust him, and that he faced Horikita once during the summer vacation and knows her intellect.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Rescues her from the gang-up, declined without heat.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Interrupts his threat display; later stands by through the Ryūen exchange.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Reads his group as trouble at a glance.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Named as the Class B leader who trusts him.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p64-1\">→ After: Ch.3: named on the Dragon roster<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p57-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ch 2  2 5  the walk through provocation arrives uninvited at the gathering with three terrified lackeys  sizes up the pond  and picks a fight with katsuragi   well  well  so many fish in this pond  i ve come to take a look for myself   unfortunately  it looks like i m with you   to katsuragi s question whether he belongs to the meeting   how about you put on a little show for me  what do you think of beauty and the beast   looking at both horikita and katsuragi  then letting out a demented little chuckle   academic ability  how droll  that kind of thing is meaningless   hmm  awful attitude  what in the world are you talking about  i can t possibly imagine  can you perhaps tell me how i am  in fact  awful","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p57-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p57-1\">Ch.2 §2.5: the walk-through provocation<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.57–60<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives uninvited at the gathering with three terrified lackeys, sizes up the pond, and picks a fight with Katsuragi.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Well, well. So many fish in this pond. I’ve come to take a look for myself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Unfortunately, it looks like I’m with you.” (to Katsuragi’s question whether he belongs to the meeting)<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “How about you put on a little show for me? What do you think of Beauty and the Beast?” (looking at both Horikita and Katsuragi, then letting out a demented little chuckle)<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Academic ability? How droll. That kind of thing is meaningless.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hmm? Awful attitude? What in the world are you talking about? I can’t possibly imagine. Can you perhaps tell me how I am, in fact, awful?”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Gestured to his crew as if to ask whether Katsuragi’s argument was believable; “their response mechanical.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> His three followers wear terrified looks and move docile — “more like a king and his servants.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The academic-society argument ends in a cold stalemate.<span class=\"pg\">p.57–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She flips her hair and turns her back on him to go inside.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p68-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.0: the café provocation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p60-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke katsuragi-kouhei ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 2  2 5  the puzzled arrival wanders into the 20 40 gathering without understanding the group structure  then reads the room fast enough to keep up   huh  hirata kun  oh  ayanokouji kun  too  what are you all doing here   hmm  group  i don t understand  i did get an email telling me to come here at this time  wow  there really are some amazing people here  huh   um  well  so  it feels like a lot of really difficult things are about to come our way   ah ha  don t worry  it s okay  like hirata kun said  all i can do is my best  oh  i haven t really had many chances to talk with katsuragi kun and ryuuen kun yet  i d like to get along with you all  too   speaking to everyone present","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p60-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p60-1\">Ch.2 §2.5: the puzzled arrival<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.60–61<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Wanders into the 20:40 gathering without understanding the group structure, then reads the room fast enough to keep up.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Huh, Hirata-kun? Oh, Ayanokouji-kun, too? What are you all doing here?”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Hmm? Group? I don’t understand. I did get an email telling me to come here at this time… Wow, there really are some amazing people here, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Um, well. So, it feels like a lot of really difficult things are about to come our way,”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Somewhat taken back yet respectful of everyone gathered; by fragments of conversation she begins to grasp the situation.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah ha! Don’t worry, it’s okay! Like Hirata-kun said, all I can do is my best. Oh, I haven’t really had many chances to talk with Katsuragi-kun and Ryuuen-kun yet. I’d like to get along with you all, too.” (speaking to everyone present)<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Delivers the last line without anxiety, disgust, displeasure, or joy in her voice.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Takes his composure as her anchor.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Names him as someone she hasn’t talked to yet.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Names him the same way, in the same breath.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Present for her cold exit.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p27-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: the hallway interrupt and the message compare<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p64-1\">→ After: Ch.3: named on the Dragon roster<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p63-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio katsuragi-kouhei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  3 0  the 8 00 cafe and the ryuen interrupt blue ocean cafe on the ship s deck at 7 55   he meets horikita for the 8 00 vip message  then ryuen and ibuki sit down uninvited and pick at the island result until the coffee is done   i was waiting for an hour   teasing horikita  she arrived before the designated time anyway   i see  this really seems like an inevitable grouping   reading horikita s dragon list   but there s probably a gap between me and the professor  same as you and hirata  there are too many details that don t fit the score theory   i suppose neither of us was chosen  then   yeah  if you re chosen  then you could lead your group to any of the outcomes   there are some things i can t yet see  like how some of the students i don t know will react  i won t know until i meet with them directly  but i thought of a way to lead us to victory   me too  can t wait to see what you do with your group  i answered   answering horikita s wish to see his results   ryuuen  i answered   his answer to who he is most wary of   of course  considering he s only a first year student  he s excellent  if you d asked me who the most excellent student was  then katsuragi would ve been my answer  but if you re asking who i m wary of  then it s ryuuen  by a mile  i answered   i think we were being spied on  him suddenly meeting up with us is too convenient  i said   maybe she was forced to keep an eye on us  or maybe she just happened to see us by chance  if that s the case  it would","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p63-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p63-1\">Ch.3 §3.0: the 8:00 café and the Ryūen interrupt<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.63–77<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Blue Ocean café on the ship’s deck at 7:55 — he meets Horikita for the 8:00 VIP message, then Ryūen and Ibuki sit down uninvited and pick at the island result until the coffee is done.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I was waiting for an hour.” (teasing Horikita; she arrived before the designated time anyway)<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I see. This really seems like an inevitable grouping,” (reading Horikita’s Dragon list)<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “But there’s probably a gap between me and the Professor, same as you and Hirata. There are too many details that don’t fit the score theory.”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>19 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads the Dragon roster as a “dream team” of class representatives — Katsuragi, Kanzaki, Ryuuen — and a death match; notes Kōenji’s abundance would not be contributed.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I suppose neither of us was chosen, then.”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. If you’re chosen, then you could lead your group to any of the outcomes,”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Weighs the VIP’s edge at 500,000 points and calls the school’s “no disadvantages” line a lie — without the VIP in the class the point gap widens.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There are some things I can’t yet see, like how some of the students I don’t know will react. I won’t know until I meet with them directly. But I thought of a way to lead us to victory.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Me too. Can’t wait to see what you do with your group,” I answered. (answering Horikita’s wish to see his results)<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ryuuen,” I answered. (his answer to who he is most wary of)<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course. Considering he’s only a first-year student, he’s excellent. If you’d asked me who the most excellent student was, then Katsuragi would’ve been my answer. But if you’re asking who I’m wary of, then it’s Ryuuen, by a mile,” I answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Marks Mashima’s earlier “after thorough consideration” phrasing as proof the VIP was chosen by a rule, not a roll.<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Silences Horikita with a finger on her lips the moment Ryūen’s shadow appears.<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think we were being spied on. Him suddenly meeting up with us is too convenient,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Maybe she was forced to keep an eye on us, or maybe she just happened to see us by chance. If that’s the case, it would help us,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A mistake,” I muttered. (after Ryūen’s “someone just like him” line lands too easily)<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think we’re done for the time being. I’m still sleepy, so I’m going to head back to my room,” I muttered.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Works the whole café as cover: feeds Horikita the strategy he will not show Ryūen, then reads the encounter as a possible leak and files it away.<span class=\"pg\">p.63–76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The morning partner; he teases, trades wary-lists, and parts with her report request.<span class=\"pg\">p.63–77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Faces the man he called his top wary name; knows Ryūen suspects him and that the meeting itself may have given the hint away.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> She is his Rabbit groupmate and, he suspects, Ryūen’s lookout.<span class=\"pg\">p.68, 76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Names him the most excellent first-year, but not the one he fears.<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.5: the 20:40 gathering<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p78-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: observing the Rabbit group<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p63-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio katsuragi-kouhei hirata-yousuke kushida-kikyou sakayanagi-arisu horikita-suzune","q":"ch 3  3 0  the blue ocean briefing meets ayanokoji at the empty blue ocean cafe an hour early  hands over her memorized dragon group list at 8 00  and holds the table through ryuen s interrupt   you re rather early   that s not my problem  as i ve still arrived before the designated time  besides  how would i know if you d been waiting even ten hours or more   you mean ichinose san being in your group  don t you  i suppose only the class b students know if she s really excellent or not  a leader s qualities and level of excellence aren t necessarily directly proportional  said horikita   from what we can deduce  i wonder if there s a certain method they re using to sort us into the twelve groups  ayanokouji kun  your grades are very similar to karuizawa san s  are they grouping us based on our scores  oh  but yukimura kun has high academic ability  and so does kouenji kun  they re at the top of the class  said horikita   no  we weren t chosen  i m not sure if we should be happy or sad   even so  i don t like how they wrote it  it s like they re saying i m not qualified to be the vip   i look forward to your results  said horikita   for the sake of reference  who are you most wary of  based on how things have been going  i wanted your thoughts  said horikita   that was fast   on his instant  ryuuen   what about katsuragi kun  it s because of him that class a managed to quickly hold down that prime spot on the island  isn t he someone worth watching   i m curious about some thi","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p63-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p63-1\">Ch.3 §3.0: the Blue Ocean briefing<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.63–77<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Ayanokōji at the empty Blue Ocean café an hour early, hands over her memorized Dragon group list at 8:00, and holds the table through Ryūen’s interrupt.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+1 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “You’re rather early.”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “That’s not my problem, as I’ve still arrived before the designated time. Besides, how would I know if you’d been waiting even ten hours or more?”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “You mean Ichinose-san being in your group, don’t you? I suppose only the Class B students know if she’s really excellent or not. A leader’s qualities and level of excellence aren’t necessarily directly proportional,” said…”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>42 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narrator calls her one of the very few people at this school he could call a friend — and a thorn because she knows something about his hidden life.<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hands Ayanokōji a slip of paper: the Dragon roster she wrote and memorized, biased “to the point where I can’t imagine it’s a coincidence.”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You mean Ichinose-san being in your group, don’t you? I suppose only the Class B students know if she’s really excellent or not. A leader’s qualities and level of excellence aren’t necessarily directly proportional,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “From what we can deduce, I wonder if there’s a certain method they’re using to sort us into the twelve groups? Ayanokouji-kun, your grades are very similar to Karuizawa-san’s. Are they grouping us based on our scores? Oh, but Yukimura-kun has high academic ability, and so does Kouenji-kun. They’re at the top of the class,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, we weren’t chosen. I’m not sure if we should be happy or sad.”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even so, I don’t like how they wrote it. It’s like they’re saying I’m not qualified to be the VIP.”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I look forward to your results,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For the sake of reference, who are you most wary of? Based on how things have been going, I wanted your thoughts,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That was fast.” (on his instant “Ryuuen”)<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What about Katsuragi-kun? It’s because of him that Class A managed to quickly hold down that prime spot on the island. Isn’t he someone worth watching?”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m curious about some things concerning the VIP’s identity. Even after reading the message and thinking about it, did you notice any unnatural-sounding phrases in the school’s email? And the strict—” Horikita said. (cut off by Ayanokōji’s finger)<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve warned you not to call me by my first name, Ryuuen-kun. Also, considering you were a turncoat who only pretended to be our friend, it’s odd you’d show your face, Ibuki-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “As if I would tell you. Perhaps you’d like to tell us about your message?” Horikita responded.<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have nothing to tell you,” Horikita responded.<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Regrettably, I must decline your offer. Violent actions are considered a violation of the test rules. If you do happen to strike me, I will not hesitate to report it to the school. At any rate, please feel free to do whatever you please,” she said flatly.<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Since we’re all together, how about we have some coffee? It seems a good time to enjoy a nice cup,” Horikita offered.<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Narration credits her acting: she never shakes, and probably does not think of it as acting.<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, that’s understandable. He couldn’t have guessed that someone from Class D would do so well. Isn’t that why you and Ibuki-san are here? You came to check on me. Am I wrong?” asked Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course,” Horikita answered, sipping her coffee. She seemed at ease, which was unusual.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Think whatever you like. Though I wonder…how did you figure out my strategy? You only saw the results of the test. How do you know the way in which points were gained and lost? Those details are supposed to be unknown,” countered Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you think that was hard to deduce? Any idiot could have figured that out if they thought about it for a minute. Even Katsuragi-kun, who you’ve been making fun of,” answered Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is it possible that I’d simply taken the proper precautions? Preparing for the unknown is absolutely basic logic. The moment Ibuki-san met Class D, I took all possibilities into account. You were so confident, but your argument ended up being flimsy. You’ve said nothing surprising,” responded Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.72–73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m afraid I can’t understand you at all. I have no close friends. The closest I have would be Ayanokouji-kun here, and he’s always dragging me down. I’d be hard-pressed to say that he’s working with me. Sad, but true,” answered Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Draws fire onto Ayanokōji to make him look useless — “Well done,” the narration says — while denying the second-leader theory.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, if we did change leaders, he wouldn’t be the most likely candidate.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I’m sorry, but what you’re saying is complete nonsense. … Does it embarrass you that a girl managed to see through your … schemes?” asked Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.73-74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My goodness, that was rather thoughtful,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It sounds like you really want to believe that we have a secret weapon in our class,” observed Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Snaps when Ryūen photographs her without permission: “Don’t take my photo without permission!”<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, isn’t that a good thing? I don’t particularly care. Besides, if you just arbitrarily jump to conclusions, why bother badgering me to confirm them?” asked Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let me ask you something. I know it hurts that I saw through you, but why are you so fixated on me? Aren’t you concerned about anyone else? Like Ichinose-san, or Katsuragi-kun? Going by the rumors, there’s someone named Sakayanagi, too. Shouldn’t the people in the classes above C be your concern? You should be able to at least answer that, I think,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Not really. It’s just that I hate your sarcastic way of speaking. I’ve always aimed to reach Class A, so I assumed I’d be attracting a lot of attention,” she answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Really? I think he just doesn’t like that I found him out, and wanted to trick me into revealing the truth. I can’t imagine he narrowed down the list of potential candidates to you. Besides, even if he knew your identity, you’d be the only one in trouble,” replied Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.75–76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re overthinking things. No one thinks you’re involved. Despite what he said, he thinks you’re an ordinary person, considering your lackluster achievements in the first semester,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Discussion is likely useless from here on out. We’ll go our separate ways. Anyway, excellent work. If you make any progress, give me a report.”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The morning partner; hands him the list, takes his wary-name, and closes with a standing report request.<span class=\"pg\">p.63–77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The full confrontation — first name, spy, island result, photo — and she never leaves the seat until he does.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Names the turncoat, declines the rematch on rules, and offers her coffee.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The dream-team anchor, the worth-watching rival, and the man Ryūen says still credits her with the island win.<span class=\"pg\">p.64, 67, 70, 72–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Dragon groupmate named on her list.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Dragon groupmate named on her list.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> The rumoured name she throws at Ryūen to break his focus.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p51-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.5: the Katsuragi warning and the cold exit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p115-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the confused-call message<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p64-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou ichinose-honami hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 3  named on the dragon roster and in the ichinose comparison roster line only in the cafe half  p 84 he appears as a comparison point inside the rabbit room","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p64-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p64-1\">Ch.3: named on the Dragon roster and in the Ichinose comparison<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.64, p.84<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Roster line only in the café half; p.84 he appears as a comparison point inside the Rabbit room.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Dragon groupmate with Kushida — “both excellent students, and representatives of our class”; with Horikita they are the strongest hand Class D could deal.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ichinose’s persuasion is contrasted with his and Kushida’s: even they “might find themselves outmatched, despite their overabundance of friends.”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Dragon groupmate on the biased list.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> The other Class D name on the Dragon roster.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Named in her praise as a floor under her people-work.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.5: the 20:40 gathering<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p112-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.5: the trusted conduit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p64-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune kanzaki-ryuuji","q":"ch 3  named on the dragon roster one roster line   class b s dragon seat","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p64-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html#sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p64-1\">Ch.3: named on the Dragon roster<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.64<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">One roster line — Class B’s Dragon seat.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Listed among Horikita’s Dragon group (Class B: Andou, Kanzaki, Tsube); Ayanokōji flags him as one of the class representatives that makes the list a dream team.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Dragon groupmate on the biased list.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v4-p56-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.5: the Class B interlude<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p64-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru machida-kouji ichinose-honami katsuragi-kouhei","q":"ch 3  named as the island strategist and the no discussion plan never in the room this half   he anchors horikita s dragon list  ryuen s cafe autopsy  and the whole rabbit debate as the man whose fairness strategy machida speaks for","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p64-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html#sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p64-1\">Ch.3: named as the island strategist and the no-discussion plan<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.64–67, p.70–76, p.85–88<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Never in the room this half — he anchors Horikita’s Dragon list, Ryūen’s café autopsy, and the whole Rabbit debate as the man whose fairness strategy Machida speaks for.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> First name on Horikita’s Dragon roster — Class A, with Nishikawa, Matoba and Yano.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Ayanokōji’s answer to “who are you most wary of”: Katsuragi is the most excellent first-year, Ryuuen the one he fears — “by a mile.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Ryūen reports Katsuragi was “rather cautious” of Horikita after the island.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Still thinks Horikita planned the whole island win; Ryūen says Katsuragi “probably didn’t know” the points flow and that Katsuragi “thinks you planned the whole thing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Ryūen: “Neither Katsuragi nor Ichinose is my enemy. If I wanted to crush them, I could do it any time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> The Rabbit room learns his proposal by name through Machida: don’t discuss at all, let the test pass calmly, equal points for every class.<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> The fairness argument Machida voices — VIPs distributed evenly because the school hates unfairness, island proof — is attributed to Katsuragi’s read of the test’s “trick.”<span class=\"pg\">p.86–87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Narration: his plan is the ultimate defensive move; if a VIP is in Class A, finding them becomes exceptionally difficult.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Dragon groupmate, worth-watching rival, and the island winner he still misreads.<span class=\"pg\">p.64, 67, 70, 72–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The café theme — Ryūen quotes his caution and his wrong leader call.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> Named as the author of the no-discussion strategy.<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The opponent who names and dismantles the plan in his absence.<span class=\"pg\">p.85–92<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.5: the Class A pivot on Horikita<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p106-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the calm image and the surprise reaction<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p64-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune kouenji-rokusuke","q":"ch 3  the grade theory name check two mentions in the cafe grade discussion   abundance without contribution  then top of class scores","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p64-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html#sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p64-1\">Ch.3: the grade-theory name-check<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.64–65<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Two mentions in the café grade discussion — abundance without contribution, then top-of-class scores.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji: “In terms of latent ability, Kouenji had an abundance, but he probably wouldn’t contribute any of it to the team. I didn’t know what group he was in.”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Horikita’s score theory: “Yukimura-kun has high academic ability, and so does Kouenji-kun. They’re at the top of the class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The narrator who doubts he would ever help a team.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Named in her grouping hypothesis.<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p52-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.4: absent from the room<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p112-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.5: push-ups, refusal, and the Monkey exit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p64-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 3  named on the dragon roster one roster line in horikita s hand   class d s other two dragon members with her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p64-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p64-1\">Ch.3: named on the Dragon roster<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.64<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">One roster line in Horikita’s hand — Class D’s other two Dragon members with her.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Listed with Hirata Yousuke as the Class D pair; Ayanokōji calls them “both excellent students, and representatives of our class” and the strongest hand Class D could deal.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Dragon groupmate on the biased list.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Dragon groupmate on the same line.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p60-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.5: the puzzled arrival<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p113-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.5–§3.6: the VIP name and the starlit hug<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p67-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka mashima-tomonari","q":"ch 3  the phrasing he still hears one backward glance at her briefing inside ayanokoji s vip message reading","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p67-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html#sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p67-1\">Ch.3: the phrasing he still hears<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.67<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">One backward glance at her briefing inside Ayanokōji’s VIP-message reading.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> “Mashima-sensei had said something to the same effect. The VIP had been chosen based on certain considerations. There was something about the chosen that set them apart.” — Ayanokōji folds Mashima’s words into the email’s “After thorough consideration.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> His reading of the VIP rule still runs on her briefing.<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p37-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the handout and the four outcomes<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p121-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.6: the teachers’ sofa<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p68-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune karuizawa-kei ichinose-honami ibuki-mio","q":"ch 3  3 0 3 1  the cafe shadow and the rabbit holdout walks into blue ocean at ryuen s side as the island spy horikita caught  later sits silent through the whole rabbit first discussion until ichinose calls her name   i m not so stupid that i d let someone like her see through me  things were simply more difficult because of my fever   on losing to horikita   in that case  let s have a rematch  she challenged   so what about sakayanagi  ibuki asked that  not horikita  she wanted to confirm that information herself  apparently   whatever  i don t really have anything to add  said ibuki","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p68-1\">Ch.3 §3.0–§3.1: the café shadow and the Rabbit holdout<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.68–75, p.88<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walks into Blue Ocean at Ryūen’s side as the island spy Horikita caught; later sits silent through the whole Rabbit first discussion until Ichinose calls her name.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> “I’m not so stupid that I’d let someone like her see through me. Things were simply more difficult because of my fever.” (on losing to Horikita)<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> “In that case, let’s have a rematch,” she challenged.<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> “So what about Sakayanagi?” Ibuki asked that, not Horikita. She wanted to confirm that information herself, apparently.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Closes the distance on Horikita ready to lunge, then stops — rules, and Ryūen’s leash, hold her back; “Tch!”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Clearly detests working beneath Ryūen, yet is exceptionally talented — the precise reason he chose her as the Class D spy.<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The one question she puts to Ryūen all morning; he goes silent before answering.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Sits “a little further away, as if isolating themselves” in the Rabbit circle — same posture as Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Ayanokōji expected a fight with Karuizawa over the stolen underwear; Ibuki shows no tiredness and no revenge.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Whatever. I don’t really have anything to add,” said Ibuki.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sole Class C holdout on the Katsuragi no-discussion vote — arms crossed since the test began, she does not move and does not speak until called; the others take it as her normal way.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> His lackey on the reconnaissance walk; she detests the leash but keeps it.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The spy she failed against; rematch refused on rules.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The girl whose underwear she stole on the island — they share the Rabbit room without speaking.<span class=\"pg\">p.80, 88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Answers only when Ichinose asks her by name.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p16-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: a passing mention as the culprit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p94-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: the outsider’s verdict<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p68-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ibuki-mio ayanokouji-kiyotaka katsuragi-kouhei sakayanagi-arisu ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ch 3  3 0  the cafe provocation walks into blue ocean with ibuki mid horikita briefing  straddles a vacant seat  and spends the coffee working the island result until he leaves with his lackey   nice weather  eh suzune  you having breakfast with this clingy beta male   you should have received the message already  what were the results  were you chosen as the vip   i suppose you wouldn t give anything away  but that doesn t matter  according to my information  there s no way that your farcical bumbling on the island should ve led to victory  said ryuuen   yesterday  it seemed katsuragi was rather cautious of you  he said   heh  well  i won t deny that  i came here to measure your abilities for myself  he answered   katsuragi and i think differently  when i m dealing with someone  i like to keep an eye on them   i m remembering the test on the island  the result  the process that led to it  there are only certain types of people who would ve been able to conceptualize and execute a plan like that  a girl like you is far too serious minded to have come up with it  reasoned ryuuen   katsuragi probably didn t know   his read on who grasped the points flow   at the end of the test  i wrote down your name as leader  but that was wrong  there s just one reason why that was wrong  your class leader changed right before the test ended  the only explanation  mused ryuuen   ah  however  katsuragi thinks you planned the whole thing  but was that really the case  in my opinion  you becomi","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p68-1\">Ch.3 §3.0: the café provocation<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.68–75<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walks into Blue Ocean with Ibuki mid-Horikita-briefing, straddles a vacant seat, and spends the coffee working the island result until he leaves with his lackey.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Nice weather, eh Suzune? You having breakfast with this clingy beta male?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “You should have received the message already. What were the results? Were you chosen as the VIP?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “I suppose you wouldn’t give anything away, but that doesn’t matter. According to my information, there’s no way that your farcical bumbling on the island should’ve led to victory,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>25 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yesterday, it seemed Katsuragi was rather cautious of you,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Heh. Well, I won’t deny that. I came here to measure your abilities for myself,” he answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Katsuragi and I think differently. When I’m dealing with someone, I like to keep an eye on them.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m remembering the test on the island. The result. The process that led to it. There are only certain types of people who would’ve been able to conceptualize and execute a plan like that. A girl like you is far too serious-minded to have come up with it,” reasoned Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Katsuragi probably didn’t know.” (his read on who grasped the points flow)<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “At the end of the test, I wrote down your name as leader, but that was wrong. There’s just one reason why that was wrong: Your class leader changed right before the test ended. The only explanation,” mused Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah. However, Katsuragi thinks you planned the whole thing. But was that really the case? In my opinion, you becoming the leader and then retiring were both unexpected. Besides, I had my own strategy in place. I had Ibuki infiltrate your class to find out the leader’s identity. You did nothing to counter that strategy at first,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The key question is who replaced you as leader. Personally, I think the second leader was pulling your strings from behind the scenes during the entire test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Speaks to Horikita but watches Ayanokōji the whole time — “If I appeared shaken for even an instant, he’d pounce.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I suppose that’s expected of a clingy tagalong.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That guy with you is considerably smart. Despite that, he hasn’t achieved anything significant, or gotten high grades. He has some excellent qualities, though I have my doubts,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see your point. I never imagined you’d trip me up. I’ll admit it. The results of the test shocked me,” answered Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, that’s too bad. I love surprise attacks, foul play, and subterfuge. That level of strategy was totally unexpected, but your victory high will soon come to an end. Whether it’s you, Suzune, or someone pulling the strings behind the scenes, you’re stupid. You’ve already made your best move. Class D is one or two steps behind the other classes in points. The challenge will only heat up from here. You already played your trump card during the survival test, when the game was just getting started. You couldn’t see what was in front of or behind you. I don’t think you’ll find this round as easy as last time. Tell that to whoever helped you ace the test,” warned Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What can I say? I’m quite merciful.”<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Snaps a photo of Horikita without asking, studies the sour expression, and pockets the phone satisfied.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Someone in Class D other than you is quite clever. There’s no mistake about that,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A conversation reveals many subtle things. I’m glad I could talk with you, Suzune. It’s a game to me. I’ll discover who among you is making moves behind the scenes. Everyone, including your clingy friend here, is a target,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I already know their abilities, to some extent. Neither Katsuragi nor Ichinose is my enemy. If I wanted to crush them, I could do it any time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m saving her for the final course. It’d be a waste to eat her now. Let’s go, Ibuki.” Ryuuen stood and left with his lackey. (on Sakayanagi)<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The whole visit is reconnaissance: measure Horikita, float the hidden-second-leader theory, and leave without confirming anything — narration says he only wanted to chat and pass the time amusing himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The target of the visit; he needles her, photographs her, and walks off still doubting her.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Brings her as the visible lackey and cuts her off when she would snap back.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Sizes him up as smart-but-inert and keeps him in the target set without ever addressing him directly.<span class=\"pg\">p.68, 73–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The rival whose caution and island read he quotes back at Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.70, 72, 75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Saved “for the final course” — he will not spend her now.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p57-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.5: the walk-through provocation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p115-1\">→ After: Ch.3: named twice, absent both times<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v4-p75-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune sakayanagi-arisu","q":"ch 3  the rumoured name in the cafe twice named in the ryuen horikita coffee  never present   so what about sakayanagi  ibuki asked that  not horikita  she wanted to confirm that information herself  apparently   the question is ibuki s  recorded here because the answer is about arisu   i m saving her for the final course  it d be a waste to eat her now  let s go  ibuki  ryuuen stood and left with his lackey","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v4-p75-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html#sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v4-p75-1\">Ch.3: the rumoured name in the café<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.75<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Twice named in the Ryūen–Horikita coffee, never present.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> “So what about Sakayanagi?” Ibuki asked that, not Horikita. She wanted to confirm that information herself, apparently. (the question is Ibuki’s; recorded here because the answer is about Arisu)<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> “I’m saving her for the final course. It’d be a waste to eat her now. Let’s go, Ibuki.” Ryuuen stood and left with his lackey.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Horikita’s setup: “Going by the rumors, there’s someone named Sakayanagi, too. Shouldn’t the people in the classes above C be your concern?” — Ryūen’s focus is called downright obsessive until this name breaks it.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The man who will not spend her yet.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The one who puts the rumoured name in the air.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p78-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ichinose-honami machida-kouji hamaguchi-tetsuya manabe-shiho karuizawa-kei yukimura-teruhiko sotomura-hideo ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  3 1  observing the rabbit group meets yukimura and the professor outside the rabbit room  then sits through the first group discussion as ichinose and machida trade katsuragi s no discussion plan   no  i don t have a favorite speech pattern or anything  not especially  anyway  i answered   to the professor s moe dialect question   well  professor  what about you  do you have a speech pattern you like  i asked   it s nothing  i said   on why karuizawa and ibuki sit apart   he expected a fight over the stolen underwear   i agree  too  we re a group  like you said  and we could all use some private points  if it s possible  i d like us to work together  what do you say  professor   i mean  the strategy s fine  besides  i think most people here agree  and i ve never been good at talking  i answered","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p78-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p78-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: observing the Rabbit group<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.78–93<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Yukimura and the Professor outside the Rabbit room, then sits through the first group discussion as Ichinose and Machida trade Katsuragi’s no-discussion plan.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+1 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “No, I don’t have a favorite speech pattern or anything. Not especially, anyway,” I answered. (to the Professor’s moe-dialect question)<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Well, Professor, what about you? Do you have a speech pattern you like?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “It’s nothing,” I said. (on why Karuizawa and Ibuki sit apart — he expected a fight over the stolen underwear)<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Follows the Professor’s dialect ranking as a way to kill time before the room fills.<span class=\"pg\">p.79–80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes the eleven-person circle, the class clusters, and that Karuizawa and Ibuki isolate themselves; recognizes the Class A boy who once offered him a deal to betray Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Jumps into the opening vote to bind the Professor on camera: “What do you say, Professor?”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I agree, too. We’re a group, like you said, and we could all use some private points. If it’s possible, I’d like us to work together. What do you say, Professor?”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads Ichinose’s “assume that no one here is the VIP” as a narrowing question and clocks the answer order — Ichinose, Karuizawa, Yukimura, Manabe, Hamaguchi — as the first suspect list.<span class=\"pg\">p.82–83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I mean, the strategy’s fine. Besides, I think most people here agree, and I’ve never been good at talking,” I answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Publicly backs Katsuragi’s plan while privately sure it is hiding something; lays low for the rest of the session.<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Judges the room’s low-communication types as reactive and refuses to get impatient.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Watches her take the lead, tests her with the Professor, and is last in her roll call.<span class=\"pg\">p.81–89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> Sits through the Class A pitch and the silent withdrawal.<span class=\"pg\">p.83–91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> Notes the Class B counter that holds the middle of the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.82–90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Present when she turns on Karuizawa with the Rika charge.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Shares the room with her; sees her vote, her bluntness, and the phone slap that ends the half.<span class=\"pg\">p.80–93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Walks in with him; tracks his swing from the convenient plan to Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.78, 86–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> The dialect small-talk partner outside, then the vote he drags the Professor into.<span class=\"pg\">p.78–88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p63-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.0: the 8:00 café and the Ryūen interrupt<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p94-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.2: the first discussion breaks up<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p78-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko machida-kouji manabe-shiho sotomura-hideo","q":"ch 3  3 1  the professor in rabbit meets ayanokoji and yukimura outside the rabbit room full from three heavy lunches  then sits through the first discussion as the otaku who votes the convenient way   sorry to keep you waiting  urrp  urp  if you eat three heavy meals for lunch  you ll naturally have a full belly  i considered going on a diet  but it seemed futile  said the professor   if you re not at full strength  there ll be trouble  it s like choosing a higher difficulty setting in a video game  wouldn t you say  the professor responded   oh ho  hmm  dost thou not care for my linguistic idiosyncrasies  well then  yukimura dono  what wouldst thou like  the professor seemed like he wanted to antagonize yukimura   from now on  i shall be like the protagonist who appears weak  but secretly has massive strength  i normally have no motivation  but i ll become a completely op cheater with enough power to destroy the entire world  i mean  i m just following the current trends  the professor mused   ayanokouji  there s something i wish to ask you  please give me a straight answer  said the professor   i ve considered what kind of speech patterns you might like  of course  a pleasant dialect that a cute heroine character uses would be good  said the professor   have you perhaps encountered a speech pattern that felt moe  the professor asked   of course  i ll rank them  in third place would be  even if you say so  kudo  that s the old stand by  the kansai ben  it tends to give a so","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p78-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html#sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p78-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: the Professor in Rabbit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.78–88<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Ayanokōji and Yukimura outside the Rabbit room full from three heavy lunches, then sits through the first discussion as the otaku who votes the convenient way.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “Sorry to keep you waiting! Urrp! Urp! If you eat three heavy meals for lunch, you’ll naturally have a full belly. I considered going on a diet, but it seemed futile,” said the Professor.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “If you’re not at full strength, there’ll be trouble. It’s like choosing a higher difficulty setting in a video game, wouldn’t you say?” the Professor responded.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “Oh ho! Hmm, dost thou not care for my linguistic idiosyncrasies? Well then, Yukimura-dono, what wouldst thou like?” The Professor seemed like he wanted to antagonize Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “From now on, I shall be like the protagonist who appears weak, but secretly has massive strength. I normally have no motivation, but I’ll become a completely OP cheater with enough power to destroy the entire world. I mean, I’m just following the current trends!” the Professor mused.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji. There’s something I wish to ask you. Please give me a straight answer,” said the Professor.<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve considered what kind of speech patterns you might like. Of course, a pleasant dialect that a cute heroine character uses would be good,” said the Professor.<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Have you perhaps encountered a speech pattern that felt moe?” the Professor asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course. I’ll rank them. In third place would be ‘Even if you say so, Kudo!’ That’s the old stand-by, the Kansai-ben! It tends to give a somewhat tough or crude impression, but it’s the obvious choice. It’s an essential dialect. In second place is the beautiful girl from a snowy country, the Hokkaido-ben! When they say, ‘Oh, sorry for the trouble, thanks,’ and stuff like that, it just makes me swoon! Those unique phrases are so moe they make me want to die! It also gets points because it’s not used very widely in the 2D world!” exclaimed the Professor.<span class=\"pg\">p.79–80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Dourururururururu… Coming in first place, jumping from little girls to the older sister, the universal Hakata-ben! … Those are the best three by far!” the Professor shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.79-80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The dialect ranking is pure2D fandom; Ayanokōji understands almost none of it and only kills time listening.<span class=\"pg\">p.79–80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course I’ll cooperate. I want points,” he answered. (Ayanokōji’s call-on; narration notes the mysterious-character tone is new)<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Isn’t Class A’s strategy fine, though? I cannot say that I can find any problems with it. Once the exam ends, the classes can talk amongst themselves and share the points,” said the Professor.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Has slipped back to his normal nerdy tone; his line seeds the Class C hand votes.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Raises his hand early for the no-discussion plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The hallway dialect partner, then the student he answers on cue.<span class=\"pg\">p.78–83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Antagonises him with the faux-archaic bit until Yukimura storms off.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> Votes with the Class A pitch he praises.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> His sentiment “spread to Class C” and she agrees next.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p37-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the Professor’s interjections<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p97-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.2–§3.4: hunger and the Sunrise gag<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p78-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"machida-kouji ichinose-honami sotomura-hideo ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko","q":"ch 3  3 1  from the convenient plan to ichinose storms off the professor s dialect bit  briefs the room hard  then swings through the rabbit discussion   convenient plan first  ichinose s downside last   stop talking like that  it s weird  said yukimura   whatever  i don t care  just talk normal   the time for screwing around ended yesterday  from here on out  we need to fight for ourselves and for our classes  yukimura directed that statement toward the professor  but i nodded in acknowledgement   there won t be any negatives  you mean   prompted by machida s four outcomes walk   a hidden downside  what in the world could that be  asked yukimura  sounding flustered  it didn t seem he d considered that point yet   i agree  we can t allow class a to keep securing the lead  added yukimura   i can t trust you  muttered yukimura   rejecting ichinose s alliance offer","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p78-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p78-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: from the convenient plan to Ichinose<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.78–92<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Storms off the Professor’s dialect bit, briefs the room hard, then swings through the Rabbit discussion — convenient plan first, Ichinose’s downside last.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Stop talking like that. It’s weird,” said Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Whatever, I don’t care. Just talk normal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “The time for screwing around ended yesterday. From here on out, we need to fight for ourselves and for our classes.” Yukimura directed that statement toward the Professor, but I nodded in acknowledgement.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Storms away from the Professor’s faux-archaic provocation; the other two hurry after him.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There won’t be any negatives, you mean?” (prompted by Machida’s four-outcomes walk)<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A hidden downside? What in the world could that be?” asked Yukimura, sounding flustered. It didn’t seem he’d considered that point yet.<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Face visibly stiffens when Ichinose shows the Class A always-proposes-this pattern — “like he wondered how he could have missed such a simple thing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I agree. We can’t allow Class A to keep securing the lead,” added Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t trust you,” muttered Yukimura. (rejecting Ichinose’s alliance offer)<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The swing of the half: votes with the convenient Class A plan, flinches at the hidden downside, then refuses Ichinose anyway — he wanted to avoid Class D getting the short end and could not commit to trust.<span class=\"pg\">p.86–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> First the Class A plan’s beneficiary, then its questioner.<span class=\"pg\">p.86–88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Flips to her side on the class-gap point, then rejects her alliance on trust.<span class=\"pg\">p.89–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> The dialect sparring partner; they walk into Rabbit together.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Hallway companion; one of the names Machida uses to teach the outcomes.<span class=\"pg\">p.78, 86<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p52-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.4: absent from the room<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p96-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.2–§3.5: strategy talk and the Kouenji explosion<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p80-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"manabe-shiho ibuki-mio ichinose-honami machida-kouji karuizawa-kei","q":"ch 3  3 1  the rabbit votes and manabe s phone enters the rabbit room with ayanokoji s party  isolates herself beside ibuki  votes bluntly through the strategy debate  and ends the half by knocking manabe s phone out of her hand   what the heck are you talking about  isn t that obvious  snapped karuizawa   umm  the outcome where someone figures out the vip s identity and then betrays the group  she said   answering machida s which outcome to avoid   i  to be completely honest  i m annoyed  even though you say we ll get points  whether i get any points is a separate issue  but we may get points even if we do have a discussion  i don t want to waste time fighting over what we re doing  i just want this test to be over so we can have fun","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p80-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p80-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: the Rabbit votes and Manabe’s phone<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.80–93<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Enters the Rabbit room with Ayanokōji’s party, isolates herself beside Ibuki, votes bluntly through the strategy debate, and ends the half by knocking Manabe’s phone out of her hand.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “What the heck are you talking about? Isn’t that obvious?” snapped Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Umm. The outcome where someone figures out the VIP’s identity and then betrays the group?” she said. (answering Machida’s which-outcome-to-avoid)<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “I… To be completely honest, I’m annoyed. Even though you say we’ll get points, whether I get any points is a separate issue. But we may get points even if we do have a discussion… I don’t want to waste time fighting over what…”<span class=\"pg\">p.88–89<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The line “Ugh. No matter how you look at it, we really do have the worst team.” sits immediately before “Karuizawa entered the room” with no speaker tag — the translation leaves it unassigned; her entrance follows on the same page.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Casts her eyes away on entry and sits “a little further away, as if isolating themselves”; Ayanokōji expected the Ibuki underwear fight and gets none.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Her bluntness accidentally builds the room’s hierarchy — the dam bursts and Yukimura, Manabe, then Hamaguchi pile on.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I… To be completely honest, I’m annoyed. Even though you say we’ll get points, whether I get any points is a separate issue. But we may get points even if we do have a discussion… I don’t want to waste time fighting over what we’re doing. I just want this test to be over so we can have fun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.88–89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The other students are astonished by the honesty; she wants the test over so they can have fun, not points talk.<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Looks up from her phone when Manabe opens with the Rika charge, denies knowing any Rika, then knocks the camera-phone out of Manabe’s hands — more force than she meant.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> The Class C girl who brings the summer café bullying story to her face.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Sits apart from the same girl she wronged on the island; neither starts it.<span class=\"pg\">p.80, 88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> First loud yes to Outcome #1, then the honest non-answer Ichinose has to work around.<span class=\"pg\">p.82, 88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> Answers his outcomes walk, then is named in his Class A vote count.<span class=\"pg\">p.86, 89<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p37-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the interrupter, the werewolf, the phone call<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p94-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: the phone fight resolves<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p81-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"machida-kouji hamaguchi-tetsuya katsuragi-kouhei ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko karuizawa-kei ichinose-honami","q":"ch 3  3 1  taking the lead in rabbit stands into the awkward first discussion  runs introductions over machida s objection  then leads the room against katsuragi s no discussion plan   your attention  please  i don t know most of you  but i think we ought to introduce ourselves  after all  there are probably people here who haven t met before  she said   well  if that s how you feel  machida kun  i can t force you to do anything  however  a microphone might have been installed somewhere in the room to record everything we re saying  don t you think  if that s true  it may not be an issue for just the people who don t introduce themselves  the entire group might end up shouldering the blame  warned ichinose   hey there  ayanokouji kun  looks like we re in the same group  i m looking forward to working with you  said ichinose   now that we ve finished  how do you think we should proceed  please tell me if anyone disagrees with my taking the lead  said ichinose   well  since it looks like no one especially wants the spot  i ll take the lead  to begin with  i think if there s any point that people don t understand or are worried about  we should all discuss it  if we don t  the situation will get worse over time  does anyone have any questions   there s something i d like to talk to you all about  i d like you all to assume that no one here is the vip  and i d like for us all to work together and clear this exam  in other words  i want to know if you think our best option is to p","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p81-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p81-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: taking the lead in Rabbit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.81–92<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Stands into the awkward first discussion, runs introductions over Machida’s objection, then leads the room against Katsuragi’s no-discussion plan.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Your attention, please! I don’t know most of you, but I think we ought to introduce ourselves. After all, there are probably people here who haven’t met before,” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Well, if that’s how you feel, Machida-kun, I can’t force you to do anything. However, a microphone might have been installed somewhere in the room to record everything we’re saying, don’t you think? If that’s true, it may not be…”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Hey there, Ayanokouji-kun. Looks like we’re in the same group! I’m looking forward to working with you,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>36 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Immediately volunteers as leader — the narration says it wasn’t easy to pull a group together, “but Ichinose didn’t seem to dislike her role. If anything, she seemed to be having fun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, if that’s how you feel, Machida-kun, I can’t force you to do anything. However, a microphone might have been installed somewhere in the room to record everything we’re saying, don’t you think? If that’s true, it may not be an issue for just the people who don’t introduce themselves. The entire group might end up shouldering the blame,” warned Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Now that we’ve finished, how do you think we should proceed? Please tell me if anyone disagrees with my taking the lead,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, since it looks like no one especially wants the spot, I’ll take the lead. To begin with, I think if there’s any point that people don’t understand or are worried about, we should all discuss it. If we don’t, the situation will get worse over time. Does anyone have any questions?”<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s something I’d like to talk to you all about. I’d like you all to assume that no one here is the VIP, and I’d like for us all to work together and clear this exam. In other words, I want to know if you think our best option is to pursue Outcome #1,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The opening question doubles as a trap: whoever agrees loudly is not the VIP, and the narration clocks her, Karuizawa, Yukimura, Manabe, then Hamaguchi as the first answer order.<span class=\"pg\">p.82–83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Maybe that question was too harsh?” mused Ichinose. She smiled bitterly.<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d rather not do this, but think of it this way. Sometimes we may need to make decisions based on a majority vote. People will most certainly be suspicious of those who don’t want to answer the questions, and the group might turn against them. What do you say to that?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Please don’t misunderstand me. I just want to talk. You may answer however you please, but I want everyone to step up to the plate in this test. In other words, I want you to participate,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Narration contrasts her with Horikita: same logic, but Ichinose can bring people together — tactical action with the group’s approval; not even Katsuragi or Ryūen match it, maybe not even Hirata and Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is there another way, then?” asked Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Would you mind enlightening us?” asked Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Katsuragi-kun? I see,” said Ichinose. (the instant she hears the name she understands the pitch)<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I suppose so. It’s not a bad thing if the school is the only loser,” replied Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, it’s going to be unexpectedly difficult. It might even be more difficult than solving the test through discussion. If you don’t doubt your partner, you won’t betray him or her. All the first-year students would have to adhere to that. Because the school guarantees the VIP’s anonymity, you’re asking for trust amongst your classmates. It’d be great if the VIP stepped forward and the points were shared equally with the class, but couldn’t the VIP just monopolize all of those points?”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. So, do we agree it’s as Machida-kun says? Each individual class can deal with the problem after the test has ended?” asked Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d like everyone’s opinions. Would that be all right? First, those who agree with the plan, please raise your hand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you. Lastly, we have one more person to ask.” Ichinose turned to me. “What do you think, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait. Machida-kun. Katsuragi-kun’s strategy certainly isn’t bad. With it, there’s no need to doubt, lie to, or hurt anyone. In the end, we’d receive an equal number of points. I understand the reason why many would follow this plan. However, I want you to consider something carefully. I can’t think of any downsides to this strategy, but wouldn’t you say that being in Class A allows you to propose such a strategy? There may be downsides we don’t see yet,” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narration compares her to a submarine that surfaces without a splash — the comeback is swift and incredible.<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If we assume that the classes all have an equal number of VIPs, … However, wouldn’t it be unfair to the lower level classes to make them throw … away this chance?”<span class=\"pg\">p.89-90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We don’t know how many special tests we’ll have before graduation, and the difference between Class A and the rest is remarkably clear. Class A also proposed the extreme idea of aligning all the classes back on the island. If Class A continues to recommend this strategy every time we have a test, our class positions will never change,” Ichinose continued.<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t just throw away a precious opportunity. Not even if your strategy yields solid results,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You said this wouldn’t narrow the gap between classes, but that’s not correct. There are four students from Class D, and four from Class C in our group. There are three from B and three from A. In other words, if we clear the test with the first outcome, it’s possible for the lower classes to close the gap between themselves and the higher classes, wouldn’t you agree?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If we don’t follow my strategy, we let Class A lead unopposed. … happened to be in Class A,” responded Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.90-91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Now then, what should we do?” Ichinose faced the other three classes, who were still sitting around in a circle. “I wanted to avoid excluding anyone, but there’s nothing we can do if that’s your class policy. If you want to participate, just let me know,” she said gently.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. If Rabbit’s VIP is in Class A, trying to narrow down the list of suspects won’t be easy. But in terms of sheer probability, there’s a three in four chance that the VIP’s in one of the other classes. Besides, even if we don’t know who the VIP is, if we at least know where that person is, we’ll have some options. Right?” asked Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t think it’s necessary for us to think that far ahead. Let’s just start by finding out which class the VIP is in,” replied Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is just a spur-of-the-moment idea. If we work together, we’ll come up with even better ideas later. The test’s only just begun. I think it might be better to wait a bit and take our time before deciding whose plan we’ll move forward with,” Ichinose added.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Her real aim is not the VIP name but the VIP’s class — narrow which class first, keep the lower classes’ chance to close the gap, and leave the door open for a later alliance.<span class=\"pg\">p.89–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> The debate partner: introductions, the no-discussion pitch, the silent Class A withdrawal.<span class=\"pg\">p.81–91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> Her Class B lieutenant — “We leave everything to you, Ichinose-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.82–90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Names and dismantles his strategy without him in the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.85–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Greets him by name, then calls on him last in the vote.<span class=\"pg\">p.81, 89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Pulls him toward the downside argument, then takes his trust refusal.<span class=\"pg\">p.89–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Works around her bluntness and her honest non-answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.82, 88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p39-1\">← Before: Ch.2: named on the Rabbit roster<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p94-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.2–§3.4: bystander, closer, and the Machida bait<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p81-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ichinose-honami hamaguchi-tetsuya katsuragi-kouhei karuizawa-kei yukimura-teruhiko machida-kouji","q":"ch 3  3 1  the class a no discussion pitch opens the rabbit discussion by objecting to introductions  then fronts katsuragi s  don t talk  strategy until class a withdraws to the corner of the room   is it really necessary to introduce ourselves  though  i don t think the school seriously meant that  i think it s fine if only the people who want to introduce themselves do it  right   ichinose  that question was unfair  wouldn t you say  if you say something like   assume that no one here s the vip  aren t you subtly calling the vip a villain  besides  no normal person would announce that they re going to betray anyone   that s most certainly true  in that case  i think all of us from class a will remain silent  machida crossed his arms  the other two people from class a seemed to share his attitude   nothing to offer  that s not the case at all  said machida   will this test really be settled through discussion  though  will you really discover the vip through talking  or are you going to bow your head and ask the vip to help you   there is  there s a way to clear this test easily  and come out on top  machida replied without the slightest hesitation or anxiety   of course  as a group  we ought to share valuable information  said machida   his fake altruism  per the narration   i recommend that we don t discuss things at all  he said  speaking loudly enough for everyone to hear   yes  the shortcut to victory is to avoid extraneous discussion  replied machida   it doesn t matt","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p81-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html#sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p81-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: the Class A no-discussion pitch<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.81–91<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Opens the Rabbit discussion by objecting to introductions, then fronts Katsuragi’s “don’t talk” strategy until Class A withdraws to the corner of the room.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> “Is it really necessary to introduce ourselves, though? I don’t think the school seriously meant that. I think it’s fine if only the people who want to introduce themselves do it, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> “Ichinose, that question was unfair, wouldn’t you say? If you say something like, ‘assume that no one here’s the VIP,’ aren’t you subtly calling the VIP a villain? Besides, no normal person would announce that they’re going to…”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> “That’s most certainly true. In that case, I think all of us from Class A will remain silent.” Machida crossed his arms. The other two people from Class A seemed to share his attitude.<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>26 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ichinose, that question was unfair, wouldn’t you say? If you say something like, ‘assume that no one here’s the VIP,’ aren’t you subtly calling the VIP a villain? Besides, no normal person would announce that they’re going to betray anyone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nothing to offer? That’s not the case at all,” said Machida.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Will this test really be settled through discussion, though? Will you really discover the VIP through talking? Or are you going to bow your head and ask the VIP to help you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Narration senses someone else behind Machida pulling the strings — Class A’s policy is already decided and he is not the power in the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There is. There’s a way to clear this test easily, and come out on top,” Machida replied without the slightest hesitation or anxiety.<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course. As a group, we ought to share valuable information,” said Machida. (his fake altruism, per the narration)<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I recommend that we don’t discuss things at all,” he said, speaking loudly enough for everyone to hear.<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. The shortcut to victory is to avoid extraneous discussion,” replied Machida.<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It doesn’t matter what class the VIP is in. You can most definitely win if you don’t talk. That was Katsuragi-san’s proposal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There are only four possible outcomes. You all should know what those are. Consider. Which outcome do you think we should absolutely avoid?” asked Machida. He turned toward Karuizawa, as if choosing her to answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Exactly. If a traitor emerges, that will be our downfall. Whether the traitor discovers the person or not, we lose. But what if we flip things around?” asked Machida. This time, he looked to Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Exactly. There are no consequences in the two remaining outcomes. Our class points won’t rise or fall much. However, we’d gain a lot of private points. The only one who suffers in this scenario is the school. So there’s no need to try finding the VIP. If we talk, we’ll start suspecting someone of being the VIP, and then someone might make a mistake,” said Machida.<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Think about it. The school wouldn’t distribute the VIPs unfairly. … There’s no doubt that Classes A through D are starting equally,” Machida responded.<span class=\"pg\">p.86-87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So you understand it now. If we talk amongst ourselves, we create doubt, which will tear us apart. As a result, our relationship as a group will crumble. We certainly could discover the VIP, but that strategy could inspire a traitor who wants victory for him or herself. There’s really no need for us to overthink things,” said Machida.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We in Class A have established complete trust amongst ourselves. We’re not at all worried about that. Private issues ought to be solved by that private group,” answered Machida.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s decided,” said Machida. (before Ichinose’s counter lands)<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, Ichinose. I understand what you’re trying to say, but if we follow along with what you’re proposing, there’ll be only one possible outcome. Only if everyone answers correctly will everyone in the group get a large number of points. The outcome you want isn’t going to happen. Or do you intend to discover the VIP’s identity through discussion, and then have Class B betray the rest of us? You just asked everyone if they wanted the first outcome. You aren’t very trustworthy, wouldn’t you say?” countered Machida.<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s true. But would B, a higher-level class, accept such a thing? There’s no benefit to sacrificing your class so that the classes below gain something,” Machida said.<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, you oppose our proposal. Please remember that Class A has already committed to its decision. No matter what, we will discuss anything. You may talk amongst yourselves about whatever you wish,” Machida answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> The three Class A students stand and go to the corner of the room — the demonstration of separation, planning to spend the rest of the time as they wish.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Runs the whole pitch as Katsuragi’s mouth: fair VIP distribution, no talk, no doubt, private issues private — then freezes Class A out of the circle the moment Ichinose refuses.<span class=\"pg\">p.85–91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The debate opponent; her majority-vote warning and submarine counter are what force the corner withdrawal.<span class=\"pg\">p.81–91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> The Class B boy who refuses to let the silence stand and keeps pressing him.<span class=\"pg\">p.83–85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Attributes the whole strategy to him by name — “That was Katsuragi-san’s proposal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Uses her for the first outcomes answer, then counts her in the room’s math.<span class=\"pg\">p.86, 89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Prompts him for the negatives answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p95-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1–§3.4: the fair intervention and the second-gathering snicker<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p82-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami machida-kouji katsuragi-kouhei hamaguchi-tetsuya","q":"ch 3  3 1  the class b counter first class b hand in the rabbit room  then the steady counter to machida s silence until he and ichinose hold the middle of the circle   i agree  of course  we re a group  and it s only natural for us to cooperate  said tetsuya   isn t that a perfectly valid question  though  ichinose san didn t threaten us  she didn t order us to answer  if you don t want to  you don t have to respond  he said   no  i think that your question was valid  ichinose san  their wariness   if you simply refuse to engage  then i m unconvinced you can offer anything of value  hamaguchi said   i don t know specifically why ichinose san asked that question  however  this test requires us to come to a solution through discussion  if the students from class a want to sit in silence  then we ll have to carry on without you  at the very least  why not tell us what you think we should be discussing   well  that s a rather unique idea  how exactly will we come out on top without discussing things  though  do you think we should let the vip remain anonymous  and quit while we re ahead  hamaguchi spoke up  looking mildly irritated   i can t believe this  if anything  i m starting to believe that the vip is someone from class a  are you just sharing information with the vip and taking measures to protect him or her  hamaguchi asked   i do see what you re saying  but if we don t know which class the vip belongs to  the point gap between classes could be widened further  what if t","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p82-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html#sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p82-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: the Class B counter<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.82–90<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">First Class B hand in the Rabbit room, then the steady counter to Machida’s silence until he and Ichinose hold the middle of the circle.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> “I agree, of course. We’re a group, and it’s only natural for us to cooperate,” said Tetsuya.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> “Isn’t that a perfectly valid question, though? Ichinose-san didn’t threaten us. She didn’t order us to answer. If you don’t want to, you don’t have to respond,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> “No, I think that your question was valid, Ichinose-san. Their wariness … If you simply refuse to engage, then I’m unconvinced you can offer anything of value,” Hamaguchi said.<span class=\"pg\">p.83-84<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Introduced as Hamaguchi Tetsuya — thin, somewhat androgynous, blue smooth hair; his early yes helps Ichinose’s opening trap work.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Coolly brushes aside all of Class A’s criticism; Machida isn’t fazed, having expected it.<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know specifically why Ichinose-san asked that question. However, this test requires us to come to a solution through discussion. If the students from Class A want to sit in silence, then we’ll have to carry on without you. At the very least, why not tell us what you think we should be discussing?”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narration: “Hamaguchi was right.” Machida knows it and keeps his arms crossed.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, that’s a rather unique idea. How exactly will we come out on top without discussing things, though? Do you think we should let the VIP remain anonymous, and quit while we’re ahead?” Hamaguchi spoke up, looking mildly irritated.<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t believe this. If anything, I’m starting to believe that the VIP is someone from Class A. Are you just sharing information with the VIP and taking measures to protect him or her?” Hamaguchi asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I do see what you’re saying. But if we don’t know which class the VIP belongs to, the point gap between classes could be widened further. What if the VIP’s identity is extremely biased, and all VIPs are only chosen from one or two classes? That class would get millions of points. Although our class points won’t be affected, I’m sure everyone understands the importance of private points,” responded Hamaguchi.<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The private-points argument the narration calls valid — and notes it wasn’t going to work against Katsuragi’s fairness read anyway.<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s certainly true that the school has made a point of emphasizing its commitment to fairness. If we believe that, then you’d be right,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We leave everything to you, Ichinose-san,” he replied. (trust from Class B called unshakeable; the other two B students nod)<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We agree with Ichinose-san,” said Hamaguchi.<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The lieutenant — answers for Class B and defers the rest to her.<span class=\"pg\">p.82–90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> The running opponent on introductions and the no-discussion pitch.<span class=\"pg\">p.83–85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Argues against the strategy attributed to him without naming him again after p.85.<span class=\"pg\">p.85–87<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p106-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.4: the Class B off-switch<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p82-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei sotomura-hideo ichinose-honami manabe-shiho","q":"ch 3  3 1  class c alignment and the rika charge follows karuizawa into the rabbit room s first yes  votes the convenient plan with the class c block  then crosses the circle to confront karuizawa with a summer story   i agree  everyone sharing the same answer would be the most rewarding result  but if anyone lied or betrayed us  we d be doomed  finding the vip just isn t realistic   even if the vip s in class a  would we be able to identify them  wouldn t that be difficult  she asked   refusing ichinose s alliance offer   hey  you re karuizawa san  right  there s something i wanted to ask you  said manabe   i might be mistaken  but did you have a fight with rika earlier in the summer   she s a girl from our class who wears glasses  she has her hair up in a bun  like a dango  remember her   isn t that strange  though  i m sure we heard about it  we heard that rika was bulled by a class d girl named karuizawa  rika told us you cut in line and pushed her aside when she was waiting at the cafe   the translation prints  bulled  as shown   no  not really  i m just checking to see if it s true  if it is true  though  i d like you to apologize  rika is the kind of girl to bottle everything up and stay quiet  so it s up to us to help her deal with situations like this   you won t mind if we check with rika then  will you  i mean  if it wasn t you  karuizawa san  then there won t be any problem  right  asked manabe","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p82-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html#sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p82-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: Class C alignment and the Rika charge<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.82–93<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Follows Karuizawa into the Rabbit room’s first yes, votes the convenient plan with the Class C block, then crosses the circle to confront Karuizawa with a summer story.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> “I agree. Everyone sharing the same answer would be the most rewarding result, but if anyone lied or betrayed us, we’d be doomed. Finding the VIP just isn’t realistic.”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> “Even if the VIP’s in Class A, would we be able to identify them? Wouldn’t that be difficult?” she asked. (refusing Ichinose’s alliance offer)<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> “Hey, you’re Karuizawa-san, right? There’s something I wanted to ask you,” said Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Her line is what spreads the Professor’s sentiment through Class C; the Class C block then raises for the no-discussion plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I might be mistaken, but…did you have a fight with Rika earlier in the summer?”<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She’s a girl from our class who wears glasses. She has her hair up in a bun, like a dango. Remember her?”<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Isn’t that strange, though? I’m sure we heard about it. We heard that Rika was bulled by a Class D girl named Karuizawa. Rika told us you cut in line and pushed her aside when she was waiting at the café.” (the translation prints “bulled” as shown)<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, not really. I’m just checking to see if it’s true. If it is true, though, I’d like you to apologize. Rika is the kind of girl to bottle everything up and stay quiet, so it’s up to us to help her deal with situations like this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You won’t mind if we check with Rika then, will you? I mean, if it wasn’t you, Karuizawa-san, then there won’t be any problem, right?” asked Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Turns her phone’s camera toward Karuizawa after the denials — then the phone is knocked out of her hands.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The victim is named only “Rika”; no surname is printed on this page.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Brings the summer café bullying story to her face and gets the phone slap for it.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> Votes the same way after his line lands on Class C.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> First aligns with the convenient plan, then refuses the alliance.<span class=\"pg\">p.88, 92<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p94-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1–§3.4: beaten back, then handed the fuse<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p94-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"manabe-shiho karuizawa-kei sakura-airi yukimura-teruhiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  3 2  the first discussion breaks up watches the manabe karuizawa phone fight resolve through machida s intervention  then leaves with the group and decides to pull sakura for a second opinion on the test   well  we re heading back  too  i want to talk to hirata about some things  i said   cover for slipping away   hey  yukimura  wasn t karuizawa acting strangely  i asked   hmm  perfect timing  i murmured   sakura s instant message","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p94-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p94-1\">Ch.3 §3.2: the first discussion breaks up<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.94–97<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Watches the Manabe–Karuizawa phone fight resolve through Machida’s intervention, then leaves with the group and decides to pull Sakura for a second opinion on the test.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Well, we’re heading back, too. I want to talk to Hirata about some things,” I said. (cover for slipping away)<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Hey, Yukimura. Wasn’t Karuizawa acting strangely?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Hmm. Perfect timing,” I murmured. (Sakura’s instant message)<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stays out of the middle of Manabe’s glare — “I didn’t want to get caught in the middle of anything, so I averted my eyes and got out of there.”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Wants opinions from people other than Hirata and Horikita — “I’d probably gain insight after learning more about Sakura’s group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Keeps clear of her after the phone slap.<span class=\"pg\">p.94–96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Reads the fear under her tough-girl act as off, then asks Yukimura about it.<span class=\"pg\">p.94, 97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Answers her meet-up message and heads for the bow.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Asks him first about Karuizawa’s mood.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p78-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: observing the Rabbit group<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p97-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.2: the bow with Sakura<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p94-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"manabe-shiho karuizawa-kei ibuki-mio","q":"ch 3  3 1  the outsider s verdict watches the manabe karuizawa picture fight from the circle and speaks once  as an outsider   stupid  said ibuki   that s right  this absolutely has nothing to do with me  so i said what i thought as an outsider","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p94-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p94-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: the outsider’s verdict<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.94–95<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Watches the Manabe–Karuizawa picture fight from the circle and speaks once, as an outsider.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> “Stupid,” said Ibuki.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> “That’s right. This absolutely has nothing to do with me. So I said what I thought as an outsider.”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Crosses her arms and looks away; Manabe does not confront her — the narration reads a clear Class C hierarchy with Ibuki above Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Looks scornfully over at Manabe, showing her contempt, while the other Class C girls laugh at Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Above her in the Class C pecking order.<span class=\"pg\">p.94–95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The only Class C voice that does not pile on her.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v4-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.0–§3.1: the café shadow and the Rabbit holdout<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p94-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"machida-kouji ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei yukimura-teruhiko hamaguchi-tetsuya ichinose-honami","q":"ch 3  3 2 3 4  bystander  closer  and the machida bait watches the phone fight as a bystander judging who is right  closes the first session kindly  leads the gloomy second gathering and works machida through yukimura and karuizawa   well  we have five more discussion periods left  how about we bring this session to a close  ichinose spoke kindly   well  this is the second time we ve gathered like this  don t you think we should start having open  honest conversation  we ll only meet so many times  reasoned ichinose   you know  life on a ship s not bad  it s really fun  right  even though we have to get together twice a day  we re still free to chat and use our phones  it s not like class  said ichinose   right  so  that s why we need to get more comfortable  we need to talk like we re all friends  don t you think it s hard  putting up walls like that  machida kun and the others always look so stern  you know   but couldn t i say the same thing of you  machida kun  can you really trust your allies  asked ichinose   really  you know what they say  an ounce of prevention is worth a pound of cure  are you trying to tell me that no one in your class would want even one extra point  it s not like the school will be bothered if you get more  replied ichinose   hmm  i suppose this is going to be tough  what do you think  ayanokouji kun   to him after class a leaves   it s far too soon to give up  let s work hard together  ichinose seemed determined to do her best   well  even if we ","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p94-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p94-1\">Ch.3 §3.2–§3.4: bystander, closer, and the Machida bait<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.94, p.96, p.106–110<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Watches the phone fight as a bystander judging who is right; closes the first session kindly; leads the gloomy second gathering and works Machida through Yukimura and Karuizawa.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Well, we have five more discussion periods left. How about we bring this session to a close?” Ichinose spoke kindly.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Well, this is the second time we’ve gathered like this. Don’t you think we should start having open, honest conversation? We’ll only meet so many times,” reasoned Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “You know, life on a ship’s not bad. It’s really fun, right? Even though we have to get together twice a day, we’re still free to chat and use our phones. It’s not like class,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> “Ichinose watched it unfold, a bystander. It was as if she was trying to determine who was right and wrong.”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Takes the lead again; wished for peace; Class B ready to ally without hesitation — “Ichinose and her friends should have been striving for a Class B victory,” yet she pushes cross-class talk.<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Right? So, that’s why we need to get more comfortable. We need to talk like we’re all friends. Don’t you think it’s hard, putting up walls like that? Machida-kun and the others always look so stern, you know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But couldn’t I say the same thing of you, Machida-kun? Can you really trust your allies?” asked Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Really? You know what they say: An ounce of prevention is worth a pound of cure. Are you trying to tell me that no one in your class would want even one extra point? It’s not like the school will be bothered if you get more,” replied Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Smiles at Machida’s “That’s stupid” — she’d “certainly gotten a response out of him”; the narration calls the Yukimura–Karuizawa pair her information-collecting tools and wonders when Machida will notice the ploy.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hmm. I suppose this is going to be tough. What do you think, Ayanokouji-kun?” (to him after Class A leaves)<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s far too soon to give up. Let’s work hard together!” Ichinose seemed determined to do her best.<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, even if we keep having these discussions, I don’t think anyone will come out and say they’re the VIP. The benefits of staying hidden are just too great, same as the downsides for being discovered. At this rate, Class A’s worst-case scenario prediction will probably come true,” said Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narrator: calmer, wittier, clearer than he’d thought; if she were his classmate he would have had a crush — “She was just that charming” — rivaling Kushida in popularity.<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> The baited Class A debater.<span class=\"pg\">p.107–108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Pulls him into the walk-out talk without putting him on the spot earlier.<span class=\"pg\">p.109–110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Uses her complaint as the opening for the comfort speech.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The other half of the information pair.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> Closes the session with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v4-p81-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: taking the lead in Rabbit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p94-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"manabe-shiho machida-kouji ibuki-mio karuizawa-kei","q":"ch 3  3 1  the phone fight resolves after the slap  both sides claim the other is wrong  machida talks manabe down  karuizawa apologises for the stepped foot  and the friction is filed for later   that s what i should be saying  don t just take pictures of me without permission  i already told you that you had the wrong person  karuizawa snapped   i don t know  just ask the school for a new one  answered karuizawa   on whether the phone is broken   what  are you saying i m the bad guy here  asked karuizawa   but i don t want you to   no  i don t want you to  come on  please  say something to her  karuizawa pleaded  for some reason  she turned to machida  begging him to intervene   i won t forgive you if you take my picture without permission  what do you think  machida kun   come on  lay off me  thank you  machida kun  said karuizawa   well  i m going to head back aaah   exhausted rise that becomes the foot step","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p94-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p94-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: the phone fight resolves<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.94–96<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After the slap, both sides claim the other is wrong; Machida talks Manabe down, Karuizawa apologises for the stepped foot, and the friction is filed for later.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “That’s what I should be saying! Don’t just take pictures of me without permission. I already told you that you had the wrong person,” Karuizawa snapped.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “I don’t know! Just ask the school for a new one,” answered Karuizawa. (on whether the phone is broken)<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “What? Are you saying I’m the bad guy here?” asked Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But I don’t want you to.”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Her words are “surprisingly weak” — some fear mixed in with the tough-girl act; Ayanokōji files it as maybe imagination.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I don’t want you to! Come on. Please, say something to her,” Karuizawa pleaded. For some reason, she turned to Machida, begging him to intervene. “I won’t forgive you if you take my picture without permission. What do you think, Machida-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Come on, lay off me. Thank you, Machida-kun,” said Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Looks up at Machida “her eyes full of gratitude”; the narration floats a new-love joke — she already has Hirata — then files the Class C friction as future trouble.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I’m going to head back—Aaah?!” (exhausted rise that becomes the foot-step)<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Pitched forward, staggered onto Manabe’s foot, apologised quickly and left — “Ah, I didn’t mean to do that. I’m sorry,” Karuizawa mumbled.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> The fight, the forgiveness-ask, and the accidental foot-step on the way out.<span class=\"pg\">p.94–96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> The Class A boy she begs and thanks.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Ibuki’s scorn for Manabe is the only Class C support she gets.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p80-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: the Rabbit votes and Manabe’s phone<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p107-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.4: the background-character file<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p94-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei machida-kouji ibuki-mio manabe-shiho","q":"ch 3  3 1 3 4  beaten back  then handed the fuse after the phone is knocked down  presses the picture demand with two class c girls  loses to machida s fairness argument  takes the stepped foot  then meets ayanokoji s elevator lie   what the hell  shouted manabe   what ll you do if my phone s broken  shouted manabe   i have some really precious photos stored on that phone  though   if it wasn t you  you wouldn t get all angry and deny it like that  right  let us take your picture  said manabe   perhaps the reason you re denying it so much is because it s true  asked manabe   anyway  just let me take your picture  shouted manabe   m machida kun  this has nothing to do with you  answered manabe   ouch  shouted manabe   when karuizawa steps on her foot   hey  what the hell  shouted manabe   yelling at the room as they leave","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p94-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html#sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p94-1\">Ch.3 §3.1–§3.4: beaten back, then handed the fuse<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.94–96, p.110–111<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After the phone is knocked down, presses the picture demand with two Class C girls, loses to Machida’s fairness argument, takes the stepped foot, then meets Ayanokōji’s elevator lie.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> “What the hell?!” shouted Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> “What’ll you do if my phone’s broken?” shouted Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> “I have some really precious photos stored on that phone, though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If it wasn’t you, you wouldn’t get all angry and deny it like that, right? Let us take your picture,” said Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Perhaps the reason you’re denying it so much is because it’s true?” asked Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Points her phone camera at Karuizawa to force the picture while two other Class C girls laugh; Ibuki’s “Stupid” is the only pushback and Manabe does not confront her — Class C hierarchy, Ibuki above her.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Anyway, just let me take your picture!” shouted Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “M-Machida-kun, this has nothing to do with you,” answered Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Backed down by Machida’s fairness argument without being wholly convinced.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ouch!” shouted Manabe. (when Karuizawa steps on her foot)<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, what the hell?!” shouted Manabe. (yelling at the room as they leave)<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The picture target and the foot that lands on her.<span class=\"pg\">p.94–96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> The Class A arbiter who stops her.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Scorned as an outsider; the hierarchy keeps Manabe from answering back.<span class=\"pg\">p.94–95<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p82-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: Class C alignment and the Rika charge<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p110-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.4: the elevator fuse<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p95-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei manabe-shiho ichinose-honami morishige-takurou takemoto-shigeru machida-kouji","q":"ch 3  3 1 3 4  the fair intervention and the second gathering snicker called over by karuizawa mid fight  rules manabe in the wrong on pictures  then reappears in the second discussion as ichinose s baited target   i agree  manabe  karuizawa has told you that she doesn t want you to take her picture  stop it  machida added   from what i ve heard just now  i think you re the one in the wrong here  manabe  karuizawa told you she doesn t know what you re talking about  so it s wrong for you to forcefully take her picture  don t you agree  i think it s best to talk to your friend again and confirm if the story is true   all i did was the right thing  machida blushed slightly   after karuizawa s gratitude  narration floats a love line   she already has hirata   you re free to do whatever you want  but you probably won t find the vip    devising a way to gain points for themselves    how can you trust these guys  he asked   the snicker after ichinose s optimism   of course i can   on trusting his allies  looks at morishige beside him  then refocuses on ichinose s calm class a image   we have no reason to fuss over finding the vip  we have more than 100 000 points deposited into our accounts every month  no one in our class would lie just to get a mere 500 000   that s stupid  go ahead and keep being delusional  you re just grasping at straws","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p95-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html#sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p95-1\">Ch.3 §3.1–§3.4: the fair intervention and the second-gathering snicker<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.95, p.107–108<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Called over by Karuizawa mid-fight, rules Manabe in the wrong on pictures, then reappears in the second discussion as Ichinose’s baited target.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#morishige-takurou\">Morishige Takurō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#takemoto-shigeru\">Takemoto Shigeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> “I agree. Manabe, Karuizawa has told you that she doesn’t want you to take her picture. Stop it,” Machida added.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> “From what I’ve heard just now, I think you’re the one in the wrong here, Manabe. Karuizawa told you she doesn’t know what you’re talking about, so it’s wrong for you to forcefully take her picture. Don’t you agree? I think it’s…”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> “All I did was the right thing.” Machida blushed slightly. (after Karuizawa’s gratitude; narration floats a love line — she already has Hirata)<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “From what I’ve heard just now, I think you’re the one in the wrong here, Manabe. Karuizawa told you she doesn’t know what you’re talking about, so it’s wrong for you to forcefully take her picture. Don’t you agree? I think it’s best to talk to your friend again and confirm if the story is true.”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Judged correctly by the narrator; Takemoto and the other Class A are not interested in the sideshow.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re free to do whatever you want, but you probably won’t find the VIP. … devising a way to gain points for themselves. … How can you trust these guys?” he asked. (the snicker after Ichinose’s optimism)<span class=\"pg\">p.107-108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Trying to shake the room up — the narration says so outright.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course I can.” (on trusting his allies; looks at Morishige beside him, then refocuses on Ichinose’s calm Class A image)<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We have no reason to fuss over finding the VIP. We have more than 100,000 points deposited into our accounts every month. No one in our class would lie just to get a mere 500,000.”<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s stupid. Go ahead and keep being delusional. You’re just grasping at straws.”<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Says he will not participate, then takes Ichinose’s bait anyway — the narration notes the only problem is when he notices her ploy.<span class=\"pg\">p.107–108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The girl whose picture he defends.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> The girl he stops.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The bait partner of the second gathering.<span class=\"pg\">p.107–108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishige Takurō<\/b> The Class A seatmate he glances at on “Of course I can.”<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Takemoto Shigeru<\/b> Named in the room as the uninterested Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-machida-kouji-y1v4-p81-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: the Class A no-discussion pitch<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p96-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei yukimura-teruhiko","q":"ch 3  3 2 3 5  strategy talk and the kouenji explosion eager to start the class d strategy huddle after the first discussion  back for the second gathering and the cabin when kouenji ends the monkey group   she s always acting strangely  he replied   on karuizawa  the straightforward answer ayanokoji did not want   i don t think we need a breakthrough right now  but we do need a discussion  class a might be breaking away from this test  but i think we need to pinpoint the vip  said yukimura   i understand  karuizawa san  but doesn t that just depend on your point of view  i mean  the test on the island was also a surprise to the students  said yukimura   so you can t trust us  hirata  if you know  then i have the right to know  too  besides  if you know who a vip is  that might give us some kind of hint  we should all be sharing information with each other in the first place  it s only natural  after all  said yukimura   i see  murmured yukimura  he was careful not to say too much   after the two vip names   speaking of rabbit group  it s equally possible for the vip to be from any of the four classes  so in class d  there are two vips that we know about  there should be one more vip keeping his or her identity secret  said yukimura   you just faked being ill to get out of it   troublesome  you re not even thinking about this test at all  countered yukimura   what did you just do  kouenji  shouted yukimura   the school notification   y you ve got to be kidding me  we re despe","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p96-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p96-1\">Ch.3 §3.2–§3.5: strategy talk and the Kouenji explosion<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.96–97, p.107, p.112–115<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Eager to start the Class D strategy huddle after the first discussion; back for the second gathering and the cabin when Kouenji ends the Monkey group.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “She’s always acting strangely,” he replied. (on Karuizawa; the straightforward answer Ayanokōji did not want)<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “I don’t think we need a breakthrough right now, but we do need a discussion. Class A might be breaking away from this test, but I think we need to pinpoint the VIP,” said Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “I understand, Karuizawa-san. But doesn’t that just depend on your point of view? I mean, the test on the island was also a surprise to the students,” said Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> His words “helped motivate us somewhat”; Ayanokōji then wonders if he is the target using camouflage.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Misses the “surprise”/“Sunrise” collision with the Professor entirely.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So you can’t trust us, Hirata? If you know, then I have the right to know, too. Besides, if you know who a VIP is, that might give us some kind of hint. We should all be sharing information with each other in the first place. It’s only natural, after all,” said Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see,” murmured Yukimura. He was careful not to say too much. (after the two VIP names)<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Speaking of Rabbit Group, it’s equally possible for the VIP to be from any of the four classes. So in Class D, there are two VIPs that we know about. There should be one more VIP keeping his or her identity secret,” said Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Bolts out of his chair at Kouenji’s humming: “Kouenji, stop the happy-go-lucky act already! I’m not going to tell you to take things seriously, but you need to at least participate. We don’t want you to screw everything up like you did back on the island,” he shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You just faked being ill to get out of it!”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Troublesome? You’re not even thinking about this test at all!” countered Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What did you just do, Kouenji?!” shouted Yukimura. (the school notification)<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Y-you’ve got to be kidding me! We’re desperately trying to think of a way out of this, and that guy, he just…”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re being way too generous! That guy will screw anyone over, so long as he’s able to enjoy himself and take it easy. This sucks!” shouted Yukimura. (to Hirata’s restraint)<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Damn it. Thanks to Kouenji, things have escalated,” said Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> The target of every shout in the cabin.<span class=\"pg\">p.114–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Pushed for the VIP names, then called too generous on Kouenji.<span class=\"pg\">p.113–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Strategy partner and cabin witness.<span class=\"pg\">p.97, 112–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> His flat read on her mood.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p78-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: from the convenient plan to Ichinose<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p97-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi yamauchi-haruki ichinose-honami kanzaki-ryuuji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  3 2  the bow with sakura meets sakura behind a pillar on the quiet bow deck  she stress mutters  hands him the cow group list  and they compete over who has fewer friends   sakura  what s the matter  i asked  trying not to surprise her   i didn t really hear anything  i just got here now   so  why did you call me out here  i asked   sorry  i don t really have any friends  either  i said   by the way  there was something i wanted to ask you  sakura   has yamauchi gotten in touch with you at all since the discussion ended   for the time being  contact me if something s bothering you  you can tell me anything  i said   yeah  that s the least i can do","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p97-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p97-1\">Ch.3 §3.2: the bow with Sakura<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.97–102<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Sakura behind a pillar on the quiet bow deck; she stress-mutters, hands him the Cow group list, and they compete over who has fewer friends.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Sakura? What’s the matter?” I asked, trying not to surprise her.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I didn’t really hear anything. I just got here now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “So, why did you call me out here?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads the Cow roster — Sawada, Shimizu, Nishi, Yoshida / Kobashi, Ninomiya, Watanabe / Tokitou, Nomura, Yashima / Ike, Sakura, Sudou, Matsushita — and feels sympathy for her with Sudou and Ike as the Class D boys.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Weighs helping her secretly against acting unnaturally: “In a test like this, breaking the rules could mean death.”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry. I don’t really have any friends, either,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “By the way, there was something I wanted to ask you, Sakura.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Has Yamauchi gotten in touch with you at all since the discussion ended?”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Island after-action: he used Sakura while using Horikita, and manipulated Yamauchi with a promise of her email he had not yet asked her for — “Since I’d planted the seeds myself, if Yamauchi made a move, I would have to act.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101–102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For the time being, contact me if something’s bothering you. You can tell me anything,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. That’s the least I can do.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Watches her develop quickly since the island — more assertive, eyes sparkling — and notes she has learned to stay positive without transforming completely.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> The loner pact and the standing contact offer.<span class=\"pg\">p.98–102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> The unasked-for favour that is about to explode.<span class=\"pg\">p.101–102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> One of only two people who could help Sakura from another class — already taken by his own group.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> The other name; not available either.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p94-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.2: the first discussion breaks up<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p103-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.3: the Yamauchi redirect<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p97-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yamauchi-haruki sudou-ken ike-kanji matsushita-chiaki sakura-airi","q":"ch 3  3 2  the bow stress talk waits behind a pillar on the bow deck after moving from the crowded elevator route  mutters to herself  hands ayanokoji the cow roster  and finds the one person who will take her call   i was thinking about it  but h how do i do it  she murmured out loud   before he arrives   self talk over the wind   aaaieeeeeeeeeeee  sakura yelped  practically jumping out of her own skin  seemed like i d surprised her after all   wh wh when did you get here  how much did you hear  she asked frantically   were you listening  did you hear what i was saying  sakura shouted   um  well  you see  it s ah  i was s stressing out over the test  she shouted   i thought i might know someone from another class but amazingly enough  i don t know anyone  no one who would remotely consider me a   friend  said sakura   ah  it s okay  you don t need to apologize  it s just that i don t have any friends  sakura responded   huh  me  what is it   yamauchi kun  no  he hasn t  is something the matter  she asked   on yamauchi contact   is that okay  asked sakura   after he offers to be her contact   i ll definitely contact you  she said","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p97-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p97-1\">Ch.3 §3.2: the bow stress-talk<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.97–102<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Waits behind a pillar on the bow deck after moving from the crowded elevator route; mutters to herself, hands Ayanokōji the Cow roster, and finds the one person who will take her call.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#matsushita-chiaki\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “I was thinking about it, but…h-how do I do it?” she murmured out loud. (before he arrives — self-talk over the wind)<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “Aaaieeeeeeeeeeee!” Sakura yelped, practically jumping out of her own skin. Seemed like I’d surprised her after all. “Wh-wh-when did you get here? How much did you hear?” she asked frantically.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “Were you listening?! Did you hear what I was saying?!” Sakura shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Um, well. You see, it’s…ah… I was s-stressing out over the test!” she shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hands him a list — the Cow group names by class — looking incredibly depressed.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I thought I might know someone from another class but…amazingly enough, I don’t know anyone. No one who would remotely consider me a … friend,” said Sakura.<span class=\"pg\">p.100-101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, it’s okay. You don’t need to apologize. It’s just that…I don’t have any friends!” Sakura responded.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? Me? What is it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yamauchi-kun? No, he hasn’t. Is something the matter?” she asked. (on Yamauchi contact)<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is that okay?” asked Sakura. (after he offers to be her contact)<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll definitely contact you!” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Eyes sparkle like a child’s; a little different from her usual self — overjoyed, more vigor, maybe more assertive; the island test “changed her life in unexpected ways” and she has learned to stay positive.<span class=\"pg\">p.101–102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The loner pact, the contact offer, and the secret he keeps about Yamauchi’s email promise.<span class=\"pg\">p.98–102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Names him as not having been in touch; does not know the email promise.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> On her Cow roster as a Class D boy she is stuck with.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> The other Class D boy on the roster.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> The fourth Class D name on her list.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v4-p25-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: the roommate appeal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p97-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka sotomura-hideo","q":"ch 3  3 2 3 4  hunger and the sunrise gag last out of the first rabbit room with the class b trio and ibuki  back for the second gathering s one comic beat   i m hungry again  i wonder if there s a lunch buffet  mused the professor   if it s sunrise  leave it to me  that s my specialty  i m fired up  shouted the professor   on yukimura s  surprise","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p97-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html#sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p97-1\">Ch.3 §3.2–§3.4: hunger and the Sunrise gag<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.97, p.107<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Last out of the first Rabbit room with the Class B trio and Ibuki; back for the second gathering’s one comic beat.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “I’m hungry again. I wonder if there’s a lunch buffet,” mused the Professor.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “If it’s Sunrise, leave it to me! That’s my specialty. I’m fired up!” shouted the Professor. (on Yukimura’s “surprise”)<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narrator: how can he be hungry again after three heavy lunches in an hour — “What kind of body lets you digest all that food in just an hour?!” — and doubts the heartfelt advice will reach him.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stands up slowly to leave; last people in the room are the three Class B students and Ibuki with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The mishearing gets the narration’s flat “No, I thought. No, they said ‘surprise,’ not ‘Sunrise.’”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Leaves with him; feeds him the line he mangles.<span class=\"pg\">p.97, 107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The one who doubts the diet advice will land.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v4-p78-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: the Professor in Rabbit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p103-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"yamauchi-haruki sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  3 3  the yamauchi redirect choked by yamauchi haruki the moment he re enters the ship  the sakura email lie becomes a camera and points pep talk   wh what s the matter  i knew the reason  but asked as a formality   i never meant to go after her  well  this is kind of hard to say  but i lied to you before  i croaked   do you really think that a loner like me would know sakura s email address  i turned toward him  trying to show my sincerity   yeah  sorry   can you give me just a little more time  i asked   then are you going to make sakura tell you  i asked   you know  sakura said she hates guys that are all talk   of course she hates me  but it should be obvious why i couldn t give you her contact information  i don t want you to make the same mistake i did  yamauchi  if you forcibly asked her  it wouldn t go anywhere  it d be pointless   yeah  and i m sorry  but i know for sure that she doesn t hate you  i answered   did you know that sakura loves digital cameras  i ve heard that her camera doesn t work  and she doesn t have enough points to buy a new one  but what if you got one for her  yamauchi  if you gave it to her as a present  i asked   well  there a few options in this special test  if you were the vip and managed to make it through without being found out  or if you became a traitor and sold out your group  or if you managed to guide your group to clear the test  you d get enough points to buy tons of digital cameras  right   now  yamauchi haruki  you need to ","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p103-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p103-1\">Ch.3 §3.3: the Yamauchi redirect<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.103–105<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Choked by Yamauchi Haruki the moment he re-enters the ship; the Sakura-email lie becomes a camera-and-points pep talk.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Wh-what’s the matter?” I knew the reason, but asked as a formality.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I never meant to go after her. Well, this is kind of hard to say, but…I lied to you before,” I croaked.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Do you really think that a loner like me would know Sakura’s email address?” I turned toward him, trying to show my sincerity.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. Sorry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Can you give me just a little more time?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then are you going to make Sakura tell you?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You know, Sakura said she hates guys that are all talk.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course she hates me. But it should be obvious why I couldn’t give you her contact information. I don’t want you to make the same mistake I did, Yamauchi. If you forcibly asked her, it wouldn’t go anywhere. It’d be pointless.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. And I’m sorry. But I know for sure that she doesn’t hate you,” I answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you know that Sakura loves digital cameras? I’ve heard that her camera doesn’t work, and she doesn’t have enough points to buy a new one. But what if you got one for her, Yamauchi? If you gave it to her as a present?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, there a few options in this special test. If you were the VIP and managed to make it through without being found out, or if you became a traitor and sold out your group, or if you managed to guide your group to clear the test, you’d get enough points to buy tons of digital cameras. Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Now, Yamauchi Haruki, you need to achieve real results. Work hard, and show Sakura how manly you are. Only then would you be a guy who deserves to go out with a former idol.”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right, Yamauchi. You can definitely do it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Redirects the rage into the test as “a temporary fix”; worries Yamauchi might get too fired up and miss the VIP, then deliberately withholds the caution — a missed target is fine, the bigger picture matters more.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> The mark, the lie, and the stimulus.<span class=\"pg\">p.103–105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Her camera and her idol past become the bait; her contact stays protected.<span class=\"pg\">p.104–105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p97-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.2: the bow with Sakura<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p106-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.4: the second gathering and the Manabe fuse<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p103-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka sakura-airi yamauchi-haruki","q":"ch 3  3 3  the neck grab and the camera stimulus ambushes ayanokoji inside the ship over sakura s email  nearly chokes him  then walks out of the cabin door with a mission   what s the matter  my ass  you said you d tell me sakura s email address  for chrissakes  and you were talking with sakura just now  i knew it  you were after her all along  he shouted   wait  you lied   so  wait  so just now you were trying to ask sakura for her email address   so  you didn t know her email address at all  ayanokouji  you lied to me  he sputtered   so how d it go  did you get sakura s email address   sorry  what does that mean  i m not looking for an apology  i m looking for her email  yamauchi muttered to himself  reflecting the depth of his disappointment   how are you  how dare you trick me  he shouted   more time   show me a liar and i will show you a thief  he shouted   the proverb that shocks the narrator   yeah  that s right   on making sakura tell him   probably blinded by anger  willing to get the contact by force   you mean guys like you  ayanokouji  he shouted   on sakura hating guys that are all talk   you re just making excuses  you never knew her info in the first place  yamauchi lowered his head   but what the hell should i do  he asked   oh  she d be happy  for sure  but i don t have any points  either   so if i do my best  there s a chance i can get a new camera for sakura  he asked  yamauchi was about to burst   i ll do it  i ll do it  i ll do it  i ll do it  i ll give ","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p103-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html#sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p103-1\">Ch.3 §3.3: the neck-grab and the camera stimulus<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.103–105<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ambushes Ayanokōji inside the ship over Sakura’s email, nearly chokes him, then walks out of the cabin door with a mission.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> “‘What’s the matter’ my ass! You said you’d tell me Sakura’s email address, for chrissakes! And you were talking with Sakura just now! I knew it. You were after her all along!” he shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> “Wait. You lied?”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> “So… Wait, so just now you were trying to ask Sakura for her email address?”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Grabs Ayanokōji from behind and tightens on his neck until he taps out — “looking like some sort of oni or an asura.”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So… You didn’t know her email address at all, Ayanokouji. You lied to me?” he sputtered.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So how’d it go? Did you get Sakura’s email address?”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry? What does that mean? I’m not looking for an apology, I’m looking for her email!” Yamauchi muttered to himself, reflecting the depth of his disappointment. “How are you… How dare you trick me!” he shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “More time?! ‘Show me a liar and I will show you a thief’!” he shouted. (the proverb that shocks the narrator)<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, that’s right.” (on making Sakura tell him — probably blinded by anger, willing to get the contact by force)<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You mean guys like you, Ayanokouji?!” he shouted. (on Sakura hating guys that are all talk)<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re just making excuses. You never knew her info in the first place.” Yamauchi lowered his head.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But what the hell should I do?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, she’d be happy, for sure, but…I don’t have any points, either.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So if I do my best, there’s a chance I can get a new camera for Sakura?” he asked. Yamauchi was about to burst.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll do it, I’ll do it, I’ll do it, I’ll do it! I’ll give it everything I’ve got and win Sakura!” he shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah! I’m definitely going to win!” he shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What?” he asked. (when Ayanokōji starts “Let me tell you something, just in case…”)<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course.” (on not letting other classes beat him to the VIP)<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Blinded by anger at first, then coachable the moment the camera-and-points route appears; the narrator redirected his energy into the test as a temporary fix and worries he might fire past the target.<span class=\"pg\">p.103–105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The liar, then the coach.<span class=\"pg\">p.103–105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> The crush whose email and camera drive every line he speaks.<span class=\"pg\">p.103–105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v4-p19-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: a hypothetical at the deck restaurant<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p106-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ichinose-honami manabe-shiho karuizawa-kei machida-kouji hamaguchi-tetsuya ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  3 4  the second gathering and the manabe fuse sits the gloomy second rabbit discussion with class a absent  watches ichinose bait machida  then lies to manabe about seeing karuizawa fight to light a fuse   to be perfectly honest  i m the type to just sit things out  i m just a bystander  i said   to ichinose","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p106-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p106-1\">Ch.3 §3.4: the second gathering and the Manabe fuse<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.106–111<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sits the gloomy second Rabbit discussion with Class A absent, watches Ichinose bait Machida, then lies to Manabe about seeing Karuizawa fight to light a fuse.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “To be perfectly honest, I’m the type to just sit things out. I’m just a bystander,” I said. (to Ichinose)<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads the alliance map: only Class A guaranteed advancement, so B+D against C+A — “like putting carnivores and herbivores together in the same cage.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106–107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes Class A’s phone use is legal and calm is Katsuragi’s maintained image — “an exceptionally effective strategy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> On being a lone wolf inside Class A’s walls.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The Karuizawa write-up: off since the test started — the Ibuki reunion, the Manabe confrontation, background-character quiet where Hirata and Kushida stay themselves; she is irreplaceable for Class D cohesion and he needs to know if she is useful, “even if it meant being forceful.”<span class=\"pg\">p.108–109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Trails Manabe’s group to the elevator and plants the lie: “I’m not 100% sure, but I think I saw Karuizawa fight with a girl from another class,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Keeps it vague on purpose; had seen nothing and would have been exposed if he kept talking — “Now that the fuse was lit, Manabe and the others would react. How would the newly docile Karuizawa respond? I wanted to find out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Reads her bait of Machida through Yukimura and Karuizawa; charms him enough that he admits he would have had a crush if she were his classmate.<span class=\"pg\">p.106–110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> The liar’s target.<span class=\"pg\">p.110–111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The subject of both the write-up and the planted story.<span class=\"pg\">p.108–111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> Watches him take Ichinose’s bait despite the no-talk policy.<span class=\"pg\">p.107–108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> The Class B off-switch when the hour ends — “No, we didn’t do much of anything. Well, shall we?”<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p103-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.3: the Yamauchi redirect<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p112-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.5: the cabin, the VIP sheet, Kouenji’s exit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p106-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami hirata-yousuke hamaguchi-tetsuya","q":"ch 3  3 4  the class b off switch second gathering  named with the other class b students as ready to make alliances without hesitation  then closes the hour with the group s flip to off   no  we didn t do much of anything  well  shall we  said hamaguchi   when ichinose says they re done for today","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p106-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html#sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p106-1\">Ch.3 §3.4: the Class B off-switch<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.106, p.110<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Second gathering: named with the other Class B students as ready to make alliances without hesitation, then closes the hour with the group’s flip to OFF.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> “No, we didn’t do much of anything. Well, shall we?” said Hamaguchi. (when Ichinose says they’re done for today)<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Hamaguchi and the other Class B students were exactly like that, too. They were ready to make alliances without hesitation. It was like how Hirata operated. They were similar, but still fundamentally different.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The three Class B students relax at once “almost as if someone had flipped their switches to OFF”; Ayanokōji still does not know the deal with them or their aims.<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Follows her lead into the room and out of it.<span class=\"pg\">p.106, 110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The operating style the narration compares them to.<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hamaguchi-tetsuya-y1v4-p82-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: the Class B counter<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p106-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"machida-kouji kouenji-rokusuke katsuragi-kouhei","q":"ch 3  the calm image and the surprise reaction still not in the room   his maintained image runs class a s second gathering phones  and his name surfaces when kouenji ends a group","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p106-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html#sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p106-1\">Ch.3: the calm image and the surprise reaction<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.106, p.115<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Still not in the room — his maintained image runs Class A’s second-gathering phones, and his name surfaces when Kouenji ends a group.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> “I thought their loss during the test on the island would’ve changed them, but Katsuragi had them maintaining their calm … image. It was an exceptionally effective strategy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106-107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Named with Ryūen and Ichinose as the leaders who “would all be surprised” by Kouenji’s early traitor move — “Probably no one had imagined that someone would turn traitor so soon.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> The front man keeping the calm Class A image.<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> One of the three the Monkey exit blindsides.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p64-1\">← Before: Ch.3: named as the island strategist and the no-discussion plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p107-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka manabe-shiho hirata-yousuke kushida-kikyou karuizawa-kei","q":"ch 3  3 4  the background character file second gathering  complains the vip hunt is unfair  gets ichinose s comfort  then sighs back to her phone while ayanokoji writes her up as off pattern   but can we really find the vip by talking  i just don t think we can  it s just  like  this test is so unfair  it s too hard  the vip has way too much of an advantage  said karuizawa   sunrise  karuizawa looked puzzled   on yukimura s  surprise   well  yeah  it is pretty fun  said karuizawa   agreeing with ichinose s ship life pitch","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p107-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p107-1\">Ch.3 §3.4: the background-character file<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.107–109<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Second gathering: complains the VIP hunt is unfair, gets Ichinose’s comfort, then sighs back to her phone while Ayanokōji writes her up as off-pattern.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “But can we really find the VIP by talking? I just don’t think we can. It’s just, like, this test is so unfair. It’s too hard. The VIP has way too much of an advantage,” said Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Sunrise?” Karuizawa looked puzzled. (on Yukimura’s “surprise”)<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Well, yeah. It is pretty fun,” said Karuizawa. (agreeing with Ichinose’s ship-life pitch)<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Sighs and goes back to fiddling with her phone mid-discussion — rude in a VIP hunt, or maybe CIA-line to Hirata, the narrator jokes; either way out of character for someone who never puts in effort.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The full write-up: off since the test started — Ibuki reunion, Manabe confrontation, background character where Hirata and Kushida stay themselves; answer-then-shrink; group hierarchy would put her below Manabe and the Class C girls; for Class D cohesion “Karuizawa Kei was irreplaceable” and he expected her to dominate the field.<span class=\"pg\">p.108–109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Gets the comfort speech and the perception lesson.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The subject of the file that ends in “I needed to stir the pot.”<span class=\"pg\">p.107–109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Named as above her in the room’s hierarchy.<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The contrast who “was always Hirata.”<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> The contrast who “was always Kushida.”<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v4-p94-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: the phone fight resolves<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p110-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei manabe-shiho","q":"ch 3  3 4  the elevator fuse trailing class c out of the second discussion  ayanokoji stops her with the fabricated karuizawa cafe story   i heard about your problem with karuizawa  something about her pushing someone at the cafe  right   ayanokoji s opener  recorded here as the row that lands on her   yeah  why do you ask  snapped manabe   that s  are you sure  asked manabe  her voice was stiff  and she drew nearer","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p110-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html#sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p110-1\">Ch.3 §3.4: the elevator fuse<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.110–111<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Trailing Class C out of the second discussion, Ayanokōji stops her with the fabricated Karuizawa café story.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> “I heard about your problem with Karuizawa. Something about her pushing someone at the café, right?” (Ayanokōji’s opener; recorded here as the row that lands on her)<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> “Yeah. Why do you ask?” snapped Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> “That’s… Are you sure?” asked Manabe. Her voice was stiff, and she drew nearer.<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Goes on guard, then closer — the topic has her and two classmates focused on him “like they were checking me out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The fuse is lit; how she and the others react is left for the next pages of the volume.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The liar who chose her as the match.<span class=\"pg\">p.110–111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The subject of the planted story.<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v4-p94-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1–§3.4: beaten back, then handed the fuse<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p112-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke yukimura-teruhiko kouenji-rokusuke kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  3 5  the cabin  the vip sheet  kouenji s exit returns near midnight to hirata  yukimura and a push uping kouenji  gets the two known vip names by phone  then walks out after kouenji ends the monkey group   yeah  a bit  ah  that reminds me  i wanted to talk to you for a minute  if you have the time   oh no  that s okay  you go first  hirata  we can talk about my thing later   what  who  i asked   after hirata s two classmate vip whisper   hey  hirata  wouldn t it be better to give us that information by phone  we don t know who s listening in on our conversations  i said   it s impossible  i muttered   i m stepping out for a bit  i said","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p112-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p112-1\">Ch.3 §3.5: the cabin, the VIP sheet, Kouenji’s exit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.112–116<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Returns near midnight to Hirata, Yukimura and a push-uping Kouenji; gets the two known VIP names by phone, then walks out after Kouenji ends the Monkey group.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Yeah, a bit. Ah, that reminds me. I wanted to talk to you for a minute, if you have the time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Oh no, that’s okay. You go first, Hirata. We can talk about my thing later.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “What? Who?” I asked. (after Hirata’s two-classmate VIP whisper)<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Meant to ask Hirata about Sakayanagi — a popular guy should have information — but waits.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, Hirata. Wouldn’t it be better to give us that information by phone? We don’t know who’s listening in on our conversations,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Reads the two names Hirata turns the phone toward — Dragon/Kushida, Horse/Minami — then erases them.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Instant read: Kushida as Dragon VIP is an enormous advantage and terrifying — “Once they knew her identity, she was at their mercy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Admits his own limit: three days left, not enough eyes and ears even with Hirata and Kushida as ringleaders — “It’s impossible,” I muttered — and resolves to get more people on his side, Horikita and Sakura included.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s impossible,” I muttered.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m stepping out for a bit,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The trusted conduit for the VIP sheet; rule-reader who notes participation penalties.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Cabin partner; both read the VIP math and both erupt at Kouenji.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Watched end his own group with a traitor submission and walk into the bathroom — “Adieu.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Named Dragon VIP on the erased screen.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her message: “I’m sorry. Things seem really confusing right now. I’m going to give you a call.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> One of the few eyes-and-ears he still counts on.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p106-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.4: the second gathering and the Manabe fuse<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p117-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.6: the starlit hug and the teachers’ table<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p112-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko kouenji-rokusuke kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 3  3 5  the trusted conduit waiting when ayanokoji returns near midnight  shares the yukimura info chat  whispers the two known vips  and shows them by phone   good work today  ayanokouji kun  you re rather late  said hirata   i m sure you re tired  but if you re up for it  do you mind talking with me  he asked   the simultaneous ask with ayanokoji   huh  what did you want to ask me  said hirata   i just chatted a bit with yukimura kun  we decided to share information about the test  said hirata   i would ve been glad if kouenji kun participated  but he unfortunately declined  said hirata   kouenji is participating in a group  after all  students are required to participate  and points are taken away if a student fails to participate  said hirata   trust hirata to read the rules thoroughly   to tell you the truth  i got word that two of our classmates have been selected as the vips in their groups  he whispered   that s  i can t say  they only told me because they trust me   yeah  you re right  wait just a moment   agreeing to phone for the names   don t worry  everything is all right  said hirata   yeah  i think your logic follows  they certainly haven t talked to me about it  but they might ve consulted someone else  after all  there s a high risk of being discovered if you talk  hirata said   we still don t know anything yet  he probably had his own ideas  replied hirata   on kouenji s sudden traitor move","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p112-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p112-1\">Ch.3 §3.5: the trusted conduit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.112–115<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Waiting when Ayanokōji returns near midnight; shares the Yukimura info chat, whispers the two known VIPs, and shows them by phone.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Good work today, Ayanokouji-kun. You’re rather late,” said Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “I’m sure you’re tired, but if you’re up for it, do you mind talking with me?” he asked. (the simultaneous ask with Ayanokōji)<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Huh? What did you want to ask me?” said Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I just chatted a bit with Yukimura-kun. We decided to share information about the test,” said Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I would’ve been glad if Kouenji-kun participated, but he unfortunately declined,” said Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kouenji is participating in a group. After all, students are required to participate, and points are taken away if a student fails to participate,” said Hirata. (trust Hirata to read the rules thoroughly)<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To tell you the truth, I got word that two of our classmates have been selected as the VIPs in their groups,” he whispered.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s… I can’t say. They only told me because they trust me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, you’re right. Wait just a moment.” (agreeing to phone for the names)<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Puts two names on the screen for Yukimura and Ayanokōji — “Dragon Group, Kushida-san. Horse Group, Minami-kun.” — and erases them immediately after.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t worry. Everything is all right,” said Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. I think your logic follows. They certainly haven’t talked to me about it, but they might’ve consulted someone else. After all, there’s a high risk of being discovered if you talk,” Hirata said.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We still don’t know anything yet. He probably had his own ideas,” replied Hirata. (on Kouenji’s sudden traitor move)<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> His phone starts beeping continuously as classmates demand to know what happened; he stays the generous reader of the situation.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The info-chat partner before Ayanokōji arrived.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Declined the huddle, then ended his own group under him.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Named Dragon VIP on his screen.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Trusts him with the erased screen.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–113<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v4-p64-1\">← Before: Ch.3: named on the Dragon roster and in the Ichinose comparison<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p112-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka kouenji-rokusuke","q":"ch 3  3 5  push ups  refusal  and the monkey exit naked from the waist up doing push ups in the cabin  declines the huddle  then ends the monkey group with a traitor submission while the others watch   i did say that it was pointless to include you  ayanokouji  added kouenji  how nice   sorry  hirata boy  i m far too busy with the pursuit of physical beauty   well  i couldn t exactly help it  i was in awful shape  i couldn t force myself to do the impossible  answered kouenji   on the island   my  this test will be nothing but troublesome  wouldn t you say  kouenji sniffed   well  there isn t any point to continuing a test that isn t interesting  is there  finding a liar is simple","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p112-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html#sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p112-1\">Ch.3 §3.5: push-ups, refusal, and the Monkey exit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.112–115<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Naked from the waist up doing push-ups in the cabin, declines the huddle, then ends the Monkey group with a traitor submission while the others watch.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “I did say that it was pointless to include you, Ayanokouji,” added Kouenji. How nice.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “Sorry, Hirata Boy. I’m far too busy with the pursuit of physical beauty.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “Well, I couldn’t exactly help it. I was in awful shape. I couldn’t force myself to do the impossible,” answered Kouenji. (on the island)<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Soaked with sweat, no ordinary high schooler could keep that pace — “He really was exceptional in every way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My, this test will be nothing but troublesome, wouldn’t you say?” Kouenji sniffed.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, there isn’t any point to continuing a test that isn’t interesting, is there? Finding a liar is simple.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Phone in hand, fiddles until all four cabin residents get the school notice: the Monkey group’s test has ended; “Of course. And now, I finally have my freedom once again. Adieu.” — tosses the phone and slips into the bathroom.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Narration: remarkably perceptive and observant under the clowning — if “simple quiz to find the liar” is true, “he’d probably hit the mark.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The shouting match he mostly ignores.<span class=\"pg\">p.114–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Hirata Boy,” then the restraint he calls too generous.<span class=\"pg\">p.112, 115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Pointless to include you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p64-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the grade-theory name-check<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p113-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 3  3 5 3 6  the vip name and the starlit hug named dragon vip on hirata s erased screen  four pages later alone on the night deck among the couples  she hugs ayanokoji and flees   huh  oh  ayanokouji kun   yeah  i am  i just couldn t seem to sleep   i m fine  what about you  ayanokouji kun  are you all alone   so we re both alone  i admit  i felt a little ashamed being alone  this makes me feel better   you re already leaving   i see  well  i ll see you tomorrow  good night  ayanokouji kun   i m sorry  i i just felt so lonely  i think  she whispered   small voice after the   pause  the words hit him  like a fighter smacking me right in the jaw   s sorry  i  um i just hugged you so suddenly  ayanokouji kun  good night  she stammered   then quickly scurries away  might be blushing in the dark","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p113-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p113-1\">Ch.3 §3.5–§3.6: the VIP name and the starlit hug<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.113, p.117–121<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named Dragon VIP on Hirata’s erased screen; four pages later alone on the night deck among the couples, she hugs Ayanokōji and flees.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Huh? Oh, Ayanokouji…kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Yeah, I am. I just couldn’t seem to sleep.”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “I’m fine. What about you, Ayanokouji-kun? Are you all alone?”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> “Dragon Group, Kushida-san.” — the VIP position in the extremely well-stacked Dragon group is an enormous advantage and terrifying: “Once they knew her identity, she was at their mercy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Hirata’s reassurance rides on the three Class D Dragon members being “the best we had to offer” — they would not reveal her.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So we’re both alone? I admit, I felt a little ashamed being alone. This makes me feel better.”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re already leaving?”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. Well, I’ll see you tomorrow. Good night, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Unexpectedly wraps her arms around his chest — “Even in this cold, I felt the warmth of her body through her jersey.”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry. I…I just felt so lonely, I think,” she whispered. (small voice after the “…” pause; the words hit him “like a fighter smacking me right in the jaw”)<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “S-sorry. I, um…I just hugged you so suddenly, Ayanokouji-kun. Good night!” she stammered. (then quickly scurries away; might be blushing in the dark)<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Jersey after a bath, complimentary-shampoo scent that somehow is not that scent; alone among couples; the narrator’s chest tightens imagining a boyfriend.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The night-deck encounter and the hug neither of them can explain.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–121<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p64-1\">← Before: Ch.3: named on the Dragon roster<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p115-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"ch 3  the confused call message one message in the cabin chaos after kouenji ends the monkey group   i m sorry  things seem really confusing right now  i m going to give you a call   horikita messaged me   printed as her text","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p115-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p115-1\">Ch.3: the confused-call message<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.115<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">One message in the cabin chaos after Kouenji ends the Monkey group.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I’m sorry. Things seem really confusing right now. I’m going to give you a call.” (Horikita messaged me — printed as her text)<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Reaches him in the cabin minutes after the traitor notice; the call itself is not printed on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The recipient of the promise to call.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p63-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.0: the Blue Ocean briefing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p115-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"hoshinomiya-chie katsuragi-kouhei ichinose-honami ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ch 3  named twice  absent both times two second half mentions   the kouenji shock list and the teachers  dragon roster talk","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p115-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p115-1\">Ch.3: named twice, absent both times<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.115, p.123<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Two second-half mentions — the Kouenji shock list and the teachers’ Dragon roster talk.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> “Katsuragi, Ryuuen, and Ichinose would all be surprised by this” — grouped with them as a leader who had not imagined an early traitor.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Hoshinomiya’s Class C complaint: “If we evaluated the Class … C students properly, another student should’ve been placed into Dragon. But they threw Ryuuen in there.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122-123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> The teacher who thinks the Dragon pick was a Class C evaluation failure.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The other surprised leader on the same line.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The third name on the surprise list.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.0: the café provocation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p117-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou chabashira-sae hoshinomiya-chie mashima-tomonari ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  3 6  the starlit hug and the teachers  table wanders the dark deck alone  stumbles into kushida among the couples  takes her sudden hug  then overhears chabashira  hoshinomiya and mashima at the vending machines   that voice  kushida   are you alone  i asked  perhaps she was waiting to meet her boyfriend  just imagining that made my chest tighten and ache   i i see  i answered   aren t you cold  i asked   i m getting tired  that was a total lie  i didn t want to sleep in the slightest   good night  kushida   k k ku kushida  wh what s the matter  i squeaked   when she wraps her arms around his chest","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p117-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p117-1\">Ch.3 §3.6: the starlit hug and the teachers’ table<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.117–124<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Wanders the dark deck alone, stumbles into Kushida among the couples, takes her sudden hug, then overhears Chabashira, Hoshinomiya and Mashima at the vending machines.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “That voice… Kushida?”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Are you…alone?” I asked. Perhaps she was waiting to meet her boyfriend. Just imagining that made my chest tighten and ache.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I-I see,” I answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Aren’t you cold?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m getting tired.” That was a total lie. I didn’t want to sleep in the slightest.<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Good night, Kushida.”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “K-K-Ku…Kushida? Wh-what’s the matter?” I squeaked. (when she wraps her arms around his chest)<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Totally flustered — “I couldn’t understand what was happening” — then stands hand on chest with the warmth still there and cannot return to the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hides and draws nearer to the teachers’ sofa at the first-level vending machines.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Overhears the three homeroom teachers: Hoshinomiya’s date talk, the ten-year grudge, Ichinose deliberately kept out of Dragon and dropped into Rabbit, Ryuuen thrown into Dragon because the Class C grades would not justify another pick, and Sakagami named as part of the Class C evaluation problem.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Files the reconnaissance: “Apparently I was under heavy scrutiny.” — Hoshinomiya was watching him from the island endgame onward.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> The starlit encounter and the hug she apologises for.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> At the teachers’ table; the subject of Hoshinomiya’s “Sae-chan” needle.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> The Class B homeroom who admits removing Ichinose from Dragon and watching him.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> The third teacher; orders Hoshinomiya to stop spying on colleagues’ classes.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The student Hoshinomiya placed in Rabbit on purpose.<span class=\"pg\">p.122–123<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p112-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.5: the cabin, the VIP sheet, Kouenji’s exit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v4-p121-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ichinose-honami chabashira-sae mashima-tomonari sakagami ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka hoshinomiya-chie","q":"ch 3  3 6  the class b homeroom at the sofa with chabashira and mashima at the first level vending machines  she drinks whiskey neat  owns the ichinose to rabbit move  and is ordered to stop spying   ah ha ha  we broke up two weeks ago  i m the type of girl who breaks it off once the relationship starts getting serious  it s just like  see ya later  hoshinomiya sensei said   huh  what are you talking about  what d i do   the answer to  what are you planning  chie    speaker of the question untagged   i m not screwing around or anything  it s certainly true that as far as grades and attitude are concerned  ichinose san is number one  however  someone s true place in society cannot be measured by numbers alone  i determined that she needed a challenge  and besides  rabbits are just so cute  aren t they  the way they hop around  doesn t that suit ichinose san  hoshinomiya sensei asked   oh  are you still talking about what happened ten years ago  i thought that was all water under the bridge   the ten year grudge  speaker untagged in the exchange   recorded under her as the chie being addressed   note  keeps the gap   i genuinely thought that ichinose needed to learn a lesson  so i removed her from the dragon group  you know  by the way  sae chan  i couldn t help but notice you ve been focusing on ayanokouji kun  anyway  it s just a coincidence  coincidence  coincidence  when the island test ended and ayanokouji kun became a kind of leader  you weren t surprised at all  were you","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v4-p121-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html#sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v4-p121-1\">Ch.3 §3.6: the Class B homeroom at the sofa<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.121–123<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">With Chabashira and Mashima at the first-level vending machines, she drinks whiskey neat, owns the Ichinose-to-Rabbit move, and is ordered to stop spying.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakagami.html\">Sakagami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> “Ah ha ha! We broke up two weeks ago. I’m the type of girl who breaks it off once the relationship starts getting serious. It’s just like, see ya later!” Hoshinomiya-sensei said.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> “Huh? What are you talking about? What’d I do?” (the answer to “What are you planning, Chie?” — speaker of the question untagged)<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> “I’m not screwing around or anything. It’s certainly true that as far as grades and attitude are concerned, Ichinose-san is number one. However, someone’s true place in society cannot be measured by numbers alone. I determined…”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Also addresses Mashima as “Mashima-kun” and is called “Chie” back; most of the date-talk lines are untagged — recorded on the volume attribution list.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Pours whiskey into an empty glass and downs it in one gulp — “Must’ve been a drinker.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not screwing around or anything. It’s certainly true that as far as grades and attitude are concerned, Ichinose-san is number one. However, someone’s true place in society cannot be measured by numbers alone. I determined that she needed a challenge. And besides, rabbits are just so cute, aren’t they? The way they hop around. Doesn’t that suit Ichinose-san?” Hoshinomiya-sensei asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, are you still talking about what happened ten years ago? I thought that was all water under the bridge.” (the ten-year grudge, speaker untagged in the exchange — recorded under her as the Chie being addressed; [note] keeps the gap)<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I genuinely thought that Ichinose needed to learn a lesson, so I removed her from the Dragon group. You know? By the way, Sae-chan, I couldn’t help but notice you’ve been focusing on Ayanokouji-kun. Anyway, it’s just a coincidence. Coincidence, coincidence. When the island test ended and Ayanokouji-kun became a kind of leader, you weren’t surprised at all, were you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Agh, it’s like you don’t trust me at all. Well, I’m not the only one to blame. Sakagami-sensei is part of the problem, too. If we evaluated the Class C students properly, another student should’ve been placed into Dragon. But they threw Ryuuen in there.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Admits she is watching Ayanokōji — the reconnaissance Ayanokōji files as “Apparently I was under heavy scrutiny.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The Class B student she deliberately kept out of Dragon and put in Rabbit.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “Sae-chan” — the focus of her “coincidence” needle.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> Ordered to stop spying on colleagues’ classes.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakagami<\/b> Named as part of the Class C evaluation problem.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The Class C student “they threw” into Dragon.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The student she has been watching since the island endgame.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p121-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"hoshinomiya-chie ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka mashima-tomonari","q":"ch 3  3 6  the teachers  sofa one of three homeroom instructors on the first level sofa   chabashira with a cocktail  hoshinomiya with whiskey  mashima beside them   while ayanokouji hides and listens   ah ha ha  we broke up two weeks ago  i m the type of girl who breaks it off once the relationship starts getting serious  it s just like  see ya later  hoshinomiya sensei said   her own tagged line  kept here because the table is the scene   i m not screwing around or anything  it s certainly true that as far as grades and attitude are concerned  ichinose san is number one  however  someone s true place in society cannot be measured by numbers alone  i determined that she needed a challenge  and besides  rabbits are just so cute  aren t they  the way they hop around  doesn t that suit ichinose san  hoshinomiya sensei asked   the ichinose in rabbit admission  tagged   i see  mashima sensei nodded as though convinced of something  however  he then strictly addressed hoshinomiya sensei   there s no rule against this  but i want to be clear  stop spying on other colleagues  classes   both halves tagged to mashima","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p121-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html#sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p121-1\">Ch.3 §3.6: the teachers’ sofa<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.121–123<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">One of three homeroom instructors on the first-level sofa — Chabashira with a cocktail, Hoshinomiya with whiskey, Mashima beside them — while Ayanokouji hides and listens.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “Ah ha ha! We broke up two weeks ago. I’m the type of girl who breaks it off once the relationship starts getting serious. It’s just like, see ya later!” Hoshinomiya-sensei said. (her own tagged line; kept here because the table…”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “I’m not screwing around or anything. It’s certainly true that as far as grades and attitude are concerned, Ichinose-san is number one. However, someone’s true place in society cannot be measured by numbers alone. I determined…”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “I see.” Mashima-sensei nodded as though convinced of something. However, he then strictly addressed Hoshinomiya-sensei. “There’s no rule against this, but I want to be clear. Stop spying on other colleagues’ classes.” (both…”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The opening lines of the table are untagged in the translation: “You know, it’s been a long time since the three of us all got together.” / “It is what it is. Fate. After bouncing around from one thing to the next, we all chose the teacher’s life.” / “Enough. There’s no point talking about that.” / the Mashima playboy needle / “Chie, what happened to the man you were with?” — only Hoshinomiya’s break-up line and Mashima’s “Relax. I’m not worried about that.” are safely assigned by address or tag; the volume attribution list keeps the rest.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah ha ha! We broke up two weeks ago. I’m the type of girl who breaks it off once the relationship starts getting serious. It’s just like, see ya later!” Hoshinomiya-sensei said. (her own tagged line; kept here because the table is the scene)<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “What are you planning, Chie?” addresses Hoshinomiya; the speaker is not printed — likely Chabashira or Mashima, not assigned.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not screwing around or anything. It’s certainly true that as far as grades and attitude are concerned, Ichinose-san is number one. However, someone’s true place in society cannot be measured by numbers alone. I determined that she needed a challenge. And besides, rabbits are just so cute, aren’t they? The way they hop around. Doesn’t that suit Ichinose-san?” Hoshinomiya-sensei asked. (the Ichinose-in-Rabbit admission, tagged)<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “We wouldn’t want you to base your judgment on personal grudges.” and the ten-year-bridge exchange sit between untagged speakers at the table.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see.” Mashima-sensei nodded as though convinced of something. However, he then strictly addressed Hoshinomiya-sensei. “There’s no rule against this, but I want to be clear. Stop spying on other colleagues’ classes.” (both halves tagged to Mashima)<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hoshinomiya’s reply names Sakagami over the Class C Dragon pick and says “they threw Ryuuen in there”; the closing “That’s certainly true. This isn’t your average year. The students seem rather special.” is untagged.<span class=\"pg\">p.122–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> The drinking partner she needles and who orders her to stop spying colleagues’ classes.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> The third seat; the strict order lands on him.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Named as the student Hoshinomiya moved out of Dragon.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The student Hoshinomiya admits watching since the island.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v4-p67-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the phrasing he still hears<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
